{"step_index":4,"source":"SYSTEM","type":"SYSTEM_MESSAGE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-10T16:50:40Z","content":"The following is a <SYSTEM_MESSAGE> not actually sent by the user. It is provided by the system as important information to pay attention to.\n\n<SYSTEM_MESSAGE>\n[Message] timestamp=2026-11-10T16:50:40Z sender=b309bdae-4955-413e-bf72-299d82c5abb2 priority=MESSAGE_PRIORITY_HIGH content=DeepInvestigator pipeline completed.\n\n**Investigation Findings**:\n# Exhaustive UI/UX Comparative Investigation & Audit: Hark Pro vs. Vigil (The Open-Source Hark)\n\n## 1. Discrepancy & Verification Audit of Prior Findings\n\nAn adversarial review of the prior investigation revealed several critical factual errors, invalid line citations, spec-vs-code divergences, and an unaddressed architectural break in Vigil's frontend.\n\n### Audit Summary: Claim vs. Reality\n\n| # | Prior Investigation Claim | Evidence Cited | What the Code Actually Shows | Corrected Finding |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **1** | **Surface & Route Hierarchy**: Vigil uses a tri-surface model: Home briefing (`/`), chat canvas (`/chat`), settings sheet (`/settings`), and gate (`/pair`). | [`design.md` L18–24](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/design.md#L18-L24) | In [`App.tsx` L90–107](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/App.tsx#L90-L107), `/` is the **Public Marketing Landing Page** ([`LandingRoute.tsx`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/routes/LandingRoute.tsx)). Authenticated surfaces are scoped under **`/agent`**: Home is `/agent`, Chat is `/agent/chat`, and Settings is `/agent/settings/:section`. | The prior worker read early draft specifications from `design.md` rather than the live routing tree in `App.tsx`. Unpaired users land on the public landing page with the interactive pet, while paired users are routed to `/agent`. |\n| **2** | **Dedicated Human Approvals Route**: Vigil provides a working dedicated approval deck at `/approvals` surfaced by a chat banner. | [`ChatRoute.tsx` L90–100](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/routes/ChatRoute.tsx#L90-L100), [`approvals/data.py` L8–23](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/backend/src/modules/approvals/data.py#L8-L23) | In [`ChatRoute.tsx` L94](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/routes/ChatRoute.tsx#L94), the banner navigates to `/agent/approvals`. But **`/agent/approvals` does NOT exist in `App.tsx` router**! It hits `<Route path=\"*\" element={<Navigate to=\"/agent\" replace />} />`. Furthermore, [`HomeView.tsx` L14–16](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/components/home/HomeView.tsx#L14-L16) only renders `useCards()`, and [`useApprovals()`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/queries/approvals.ts#L9) is completely orphaned across the frontend. | The approvals UI in Vigil is currently disconnected. Clicking the approval banner redirects users to the home briefing where approvals are not rendered. The prior attempt presented this as a fully functional feature. |\n| **3** | **Motion Engine**: Vigil implements a single CSS `linear()` timing function approximating a spring with 2.8% overshoot. | [`design.md` L249–252](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/design.md#L249-L252) | In [`tokens.css` L18](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/styles/tokens.css#L18): `--ease-spring: cubic-bezier(0.25, 1, 0.5, 1);`. [`design.md` L330–333](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/design.md#L330-L333) explicitly forbade `cubic-bezier(0.25, 1, 0.5, 1)`, warning it is monotonic with no overshoot. | The code violates its own design specification. The prior report cited specification text while missing that `tokens.css` implemented the exact monotonic cubic-bezier that `design.md` prohibited. |\n| **4** | **Thinking Capsule Line Citations**: Status capsule attributes (`role=\"status\"`, `aria-live=\"polite\"`) located at `L1–100`. | [`ThinkingCapsule.tsx` L1–100](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/components/chat/ThinkingCapsule.tsx#L1-L100) | In [`ThinkingCapsule.tsx` L1080](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/components/chat/ThinkingCapsule.tsx#L1080), the status role is declared: `<div className=\"my-1.5 w-full max-w-2xl min-w-0\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\">`. Lines 1–100 are imports, type interfaces, and timeline builders. | Invalid line number citation corrected to L1080. |\n| **5** | **Audio Voice Interaction**: Web Audio API capture with 1024-point FFT analyzer \"drives live voice interactions\". | [`InputPill.tsx` L80–98](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/components/chat/InputPill.tsx#L80-L98) | In [`InputPill.tsx` L100–104](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/components/chat/InputPill.tsx#L100-L104), stopping capture explicitly executes: `setNotice('Microphone stopped. Transcription is not connected yet.')`. | The FFT analyzer only animates the bottom visual beam ([`HandoffBeam`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/components/ui/handoff-beam.tsx#L361-L380)); speech transcription is not connected. The prior report overstated audio maturity. |\n| **6** | **Color Palette**: Vigil is \"strictly monochromatic ink-on-paper with zero color accents\". | [`design.md` L7–10](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/design.md#L7-L10) | [`tokens.css` L82](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/styles/tokens.css#L82) defines `--cloud-3: rgba(232, 132, 73, 0.16)` (warm amber dawn), [`palette.ts` L16](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/components/ui/handoff-beam-utils/palette.ts#L16) defines active Bjork ember accents (`#ec5c13`), and [`design.md` L274–282](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/design.md#L274-L282) specifies blue (`#38BDF8`) and urgency red/orange. | Vigil is calm and monochrome-grounded, but intentionally incorporates calculated atmospheric and urgency accents. |\n\n---\n\n## 2. Foundational Context: Hark Pro vs. Vigil (The \"Open-Source Hark\")\n\nUnderstanding Vigil requires understanding its genesis: **Vigil is architected specifically as a private, self-hosted, open-source counterpart to Hark Pro**.\n\n* **Hark Pro**:\n  - Founded in late 2025 and launched in October 2026 by serial tech founder **Brett Adcock** (founder of Figure AI and Archer Aviation) with $700M in Series A funding at a $6B valuation.\n  - Design direction is led by **Abidur Chowdhury**, the former Apple industrial designer who unveiled the iPhone Air during Apple's September 2025 keynote.\n  - **Philosophy**: Billed as *\"An operating system for your life\"* and the *\"Macintosh GUI for AI\"*. Argues that text-only chat boxes are the archaic command-line terminal of AI, replacing them with dynamic dashboard panels, multimedia mini-apps, and a cloud computer-use engine called **Handoff**.\n  - **Infrastructure**: Proprietary multi-tenant cloud VM cluster running up to 6 simultaneous headless/headed browser sessions, with upcoming proprietary hardware planned for 2027.\n\n* **Vigil**:\n  - Directly models its design language and ergonomics on Hark: *\"the warm, pillowy friendliness of Hark\"* ([`design.md` L9](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/design.md#L9)).\n  - Directly names its audio-reactive interaction boundary **`HandoffBeam`** ([`handoff-beam.tsx` L361](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/components/ui/handoff-beam.tsx#L361)) after Hark’s Handoff agent.\n  - **Philosophy**: An uncompromised open-source, local-first alternative. Replaces Hark’s proprietary cloud browser farm with an isolated local Docker sandbox (`deploy/Dockerfile.sandbox`), cloud surveillance with local SQLite/PostgreSQL storage, and closed cloud OAuth with local cryptographic device pairing (`/pair`).\n\n---\n\n## 3. Deep UI/UX Comparative Analysis\n\n### 3.1. The Way It Responds to Tasks (Execution & Observability)\n\n#### Hark Pro: Cloud Browser Live View (\"The Window into the Machine\")\n1. **Live Visual Stream in Chat**:\n   - Rather than hiding behind an indeterminate loading spinner, Hark Pro renders a **real-time visual preview window** embedded directly into the conversational feed.\n   - Users observe the cloud VM browser navigating real websites (DoorDash, OpenTable, United Airlines, utility portals), typing into input fields, scrolling through search results, and bypassing multi-step funnels.\n   - *UX Impact*: Converts the \"black box\" anxiety of autonomous agents into high-trust visual observability.\n2. **Instant Takeover & Abort Controls**:\n   - At any point during a task, users can tap a prominent \"Take Over\" button to take direct control of the remote browser session or hit \"Cancel\" to kill execution before financial commitment.\n3. **\"Secured by Hark\" Vault**:\n   - For checkout and login funnels, sensitive credentials and payment cards are injected through an isolated, zero-knowledge encrypted Vault UI, keeping plain-text secrets out of LLM context windows.\n\n#### Vigil: Sandboxed Step Streaming, Structured Thinking & Artifacts\n1. **Deterministic Local Container Execution**:\n   - Tasks execute via an internal [`RunLoop`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/backend/src/modules/runs/loop.py) within an isolated Docker container ([`deploy/Dockerfile.sandbox`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/deploy/Dockerfile.sandbox)).\n   - Telemetry streams over cursor-based Server-Sent Events with `Last-Event-ID` resume support ([`stream.py` L1–37](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/backend/src/modules/runs/stream.py#L1-L37)).\n2. **Granular Thinking Capsule ([`ThinkingCapsule.tsx` L1080](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/components/chat/ThinkingCapsule.tsx#L1080))**:\n   - Replaces Hark's video-streamed browser window with structured textual and terminal observability.\n   - Automatically pairs `tool_call` and `tool_result` events by correlation ID ([`ThinkingCapsule.tsx` L67–158](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/components/chat/ThinkingCapsule.tsx#L67-L158)).\n   - Parses bash execution outputs with dedicated exit-code, stdout, and stderr inspectors ([`ThinkingCapsule.tsx` L273–300](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/components/chat/ThinkingCapsule.tsx#L273-L300)).\n   - Visualizes execution step duration in milliseconds and memory compaction cycles.\n3. **Decoupled Artifact Cards ([`ArtifactCard.tsx`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/components/chat/ArtifactCard.tsx))**:\n   - While Hark keeps deliverables trapped in conversation history or dedicated panels, Vigil extracts file deliverables (documents, diffs, images, data tables) into discrete, downloadable cards pinned beneath assistant responses ([`MessageItem.tsx` L197–203](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/components/chat/MessageItem.tsx#L197-L203)).\n\n---\n\n### 3.2. Proactivity & Anticipatory Design\n\n#### Hark Pro: Anticipatory Consumer Lifestyle Concierge\n- **Account Mesh & Graph Synthesis**: Hark Pro continuously monitors synced personal accounts (Gmail, Outlook, Calendar, Spotify, Strava).\n- **Proactive Trip & Errand Orchestration**: Detecting a flight confirmation email automatically prompts Hark to generate action cards for airport rides, hotel reservations matching preferences, and calendar holds.\n- **Dynamic Action Buttons**: Task completions emit single-tap action chips (e.g., *\"Order Usual from Sweetgreen\"*, *\"Pay $42.50 via Vault\"*, *\"Add Hotel to Apple Wallet\"*).\n\n#### Vigil: Calibrated Low-Arousal Triage & Morning Briefing Deck\n- **Two-Stage Jev Decision Pipeline ([`service.py` L73–154](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/backend/src/modules/triage/service.py#L73-L154))**:\n  - Ingested signals (emails, webhooks) pass through a two-stage filter to prevent token waste and user alert fatigue:\n    - **Stage 1 (Probability Gate)**: Evaluates $p(\\text{action\\_required})$, $p(\\text{is\\_bulk})$, and $p(\\text{urgency})$. If $p(\\text{action}) < 0.3$ or $p(\\text{bulk}) > 0.8$, the item is discarded with zero token spend ([`service.py` L108–109](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/backend/src/modules/triage/service.py#L108-L109)).\n    - **Stage 2 (Action Card Synthesis)**: Actionable items synthesize into [`CardCreateDTO`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/backend/src/modules/triage/service.py#L131-L143) with discrete urgency ratings (`critical`, `high`, `medium`, `low`).\n- **The Morning Deck ([`HomeView.tsx` L10–80](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/components/home/HomeView.tsx#L10-L80))**:\n  - Avoids notification badge anxiety. Mounts at `/agent` with a greeting, active watchlist summary, and a single uncrowded column of [`TaskCard`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/components/home/TaskCard.tsx#L35-L238) components.\n  - Urgent cards feature a subtle 3px urgency rail (accent for `critical`/`high`, neutral for `medium`/`low`), avoiding alarmist red washes ([`design.md` L107–113](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/design.md#L107-L113)).\n  - **Server-Driven Actions**: Strict payload-driven actions: `run`, `dismiss`, or `reply` (deep links into chat with a seeded prompt via `navigate('/agent/chat', { state: { seed, cardId } })`).\n  - **Calm Freshness**: Polling every 60 seconds with window focus refetch instead of noisy real-time websocket spam ([`design.md` L168–174](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/design.md#L168-L174)).\n\n---\n\n### 3.3. The Way It Showcases Information (Information Architecture & Visual Design)\n\n#### Hark Pro: Rich Graphical Control Center & Apple-Grade Translucency\n- **The GUI for AI**: Replaces plain text conversational histories with customizable \"Panels\" (persistent mini-dashboards for multi-week projects like travel planning, fitness tracking, or home renovation).\n- **Atmospheric Sensory Simulation**: The app backdrop dynamically renders a subtle, live simulation of the user's local weather and daylight atmosphere.\n- **Visual Hardware Pedigree**: Pillowy cards, Apple squircle corners, fluid spring transitions, and translucent controls.\n\n#### Vigil: Monochromatic Ink-on-Paper Architecture\n- **Complete Route Architecture ([`App.tsx` L90–107](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/App.tsx#L90-L107))**:\n  - `/`: Public marketing landing page featuring the interactive eye-tracking pet ([`LandingRoute.tsx`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/routes/LandingRoute.tsx)).\n  - `/pair`: Cryptographic 6-digit / QR pairing gate ([`PairRoute.tsx`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/routes/PairRoute.tsx)).\n  - `/agent`: Authenticated home briefing deck and widgets rail ([`HomeRoute.tsx`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/routes/HomeRoute.tsx)).\n  - `/agent/chat` & `/agent/chat/:sessionId`: Conversational canvas with streaming SSE ([`ChatRoute.tsx`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/routes/ChatRoute.tsx)).\n  - `/agent/settings/:section`: Route-backed frosted sheet preserving history and shareable URLs ([`SettingsRoute.tsx`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/routes/SettingsRoute.tsx)).\n- **Rejection of AI Clichés**:\n  - Explicitly bans neon gradients, futuristic cyber meshes, and emoji icons ([`design.md` L344–350](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/design.md#L344-L350)).\n  - Uses an inline 4-point SVG spark mark ([`VigilSpark`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/components/chat/MessageItem.tsx#L37-L48)), self-hosted `Plus Jakarta Sans` typography ([`tokens.css` L3–11](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/styles/tokens.css#L3-L11)), and high-contrast solid tokens.\n- **Strict Performance Budget**:\n  - Mandates **at most one `backdrop-filter` layer per viewport** to maintain 60–120fps scrolling on Linux Wayland and mobile chipsets ([`design.md` L648–666](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/design.md#L648-L666)).\n- **Mobile Stack Non-Overlap Contract**:\n  - Enforces strict z-index and padding layers ([`design.md` L521–536](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/design.md#L521-L536)): Safe area $\\rightarrow$ Input Pill ($1\\,\\text{rem}$) $\\rightarrow$ Floating Dock ($5.5\\,\\text{rem}$) $\\rightarrow$ Scroll padding ($11\\,\\text{rem}$).\n\n---\n\n### 3.4. The Way It Communicates (Tone, Voice & Presentation)\n\n#### Hark Pro\n- **Tone**: Eager, warm, proactive concierge. High-arousal consumer-lifestyle vocabulary.\n- **Presentation**: Conversational chat bubbles paired with dynamic action chips and interactive cards.\n- **Interaction Style**: Frequent check-ins, proactive suggestions, and assistive consumer prompts.\n\n#### Vigil\n- **Tone**: Editorial, low-arousal, calm, terse, and humble ([`design.md` L311–313](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/design.md#L311-L313)). Strictly bans chatbot sycophancy (*\"I'd be thrilled to help!\"*) and faux-enthusiasm.\n- **Unboxed Editorial Typography ([`MessageItem.tsx` L164–195](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/components/chat/MessageItem.tsx#L164-L195))**:\n  - User messages appear in tactile right-aligned pills ([`MessageItem.tsx` L106–124](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/components/chat/MessageItem.tsx#L106-L124)).\n  - Assistant responses **completely discard chat bubbles**. Vigil renders as unboxed, full-width editorial markdown heralded by the subtle 14px SVG spark mark.\n- **Strict Thought-Fact Segregation**:\n  - Reasoning tokens, tool arguments, and container execution telemetry never mix with the conversational prose; they remain folded inside [`ThinkingCapsule`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/components/chat/ThinkingCapsule.tsx).\n\n---\n\n### 3.5. Interactivity Deep-Dive: \"The Cat\" (Companion Mascot) vs. \"The Chat\"\n\nBecause the task query referenced *\"the interactivity of the cat and so on\"*, this analysis covers both the literal meaning (the digital companion/pet mascot in Vigil) and the typographical meaning (conversational chat interactivity).\n\n```\n         Vigil's Interactive Companion / Digital Pet (\"The Cat / Toy\")\n         [Source: web/src/components/landing/EyeTracker.tsx]\n\n                       .-\"\"\"\"-.\n                     .'  ____  '.\n                    /   /    \\   \\\n                   |   | ()() |   |   <--- 3D Spherical Eye-Tracking\n                   |    \\____/    |        (Foreshortening & Tilt)\n                    \\            /\n                     '.        .'\n                       '-....-'\n                           \\\n                         +-----------------------+\n                         | \"Hey, I see you.\"  [x]|  <--- Interactive Speech Bubble\n                         +-----------------------+       (Typewriter on Poke)\n```\n\n#### A. The Digital Companion / \"Cat\" / Mascot Interactivity\n\n1. **Hark Pro: Zero Mascot Policy**:\n   - Hark Pro deliberately has **no pet, mascot, or gamified avatar**. Abidur Chowdhury's design system adheres strictly to sleek, minimalist Apple-esque luxury computing, avoiding anything perceived as a toy.\n\n2. **Vigil: The Interactive Digital Pet ([`EyeTracker.tsx` L1–519](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/components/landing/EyeTracker.tsx#L1-L519))**:\n   - Vigil implements a digital companion, referred to explicitly in source code comments as **\"the pet\"** and **\"the toy\"** ([`EyeTracker.tsx` L86](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/components/landing/EyeTracker.tsx#L86), [`tokens.css` L281](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/styles/tokens.css#L281), [`tokens.css` L328](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/styles/tokens.css#L328)).\n   - **True 3D Spherical Projection & Eye-Tracking ([`EyeTracker.tsx` L7–22](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/components/landing/EyeTracker.tsx#L7-L22))**:\n     - Unlike standard 2D avatars that slide sticker eyes across a circle, Vigil maps two eyes to coordinates on a 3D sphere's surface.\n     - As the cursor moves across the viewport, the ball rotates in yaw and pitch. The eye rotating toward the rim foreshortens and narrows along the curve, creating an authentic 3D sphere illusion.\n     - **Performance**: Written directly to the DOM via `requestAnimationFrame` ([`EyeTracker.tsx` L21–22](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/components/landing/EyeTracker.tsx#L21-L22)); cursor movement never triggers React component re-renders. Pauses automatically when off-screen or in background tabs via `IntersectionObserver` ([`EyeTracker.tsx` L356–359](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/components/landing/EyeTracker.tsx#L356-L359)).\n   - **Autonomous Blinking & Idle Glances ([`EyeTracker.tsx` L268–275, L395–412](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/components/landing/EyeTracker.tsx#L268-L275))**:\n     - Blinks autonomously (160ms vertical squash) every 2.6–5.8 seconds. When idle, glances in random directions every 5 seconds before returning to center.\n   - **Geometric Morphing ([`EyeTracker.tsx` L113–124, L136–175](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/components/landing/EyeTracker.tsx#L113-L124))**:\n     - The body dynamically morphs between 5 shapes (`Ball`, `Circle`, `Cube`, `Pill`, `Hexagon`) using 120-ray star-polygon interpolation with elastic overshoot easing ([`EyeTracker.tsx` L456–465](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/components/landing/EyeTracker.tsx#L456-L465)).\n   - **Interactive \"Poke\" Mechanics & Speech Bubble ([`EyeTracker.tsx` L84–106, L223–242](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/components/landing/EyeTracker.tsx#L84-L106))**:\n     - Clicking or poking the pet triggers a tactile squish (`scale: 0.96` with elastic spring recovery; [`tokens.css` L286–292](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/styles/tokens.css#L286-L292)).\n     - Opens an anchored speech bubble off its lower-right corner, typing out lines letter-by-letter (38ms/char):\n       - *\"Hey, I see you.\"*\n       - *\"Boop.\"*\n       - *\"That tickles.\"*\n       - *\"Hi there!\"*\n       - *\"Stop poking me.\"*\n       - *\"I'm watching you.\"*\n       - *\"Again? Okay.\"*\n       - *\"You found me.\"*\n   - **Omnipresence**:\n     - Rendered on the public landing page hero and navbar ([`LandingRoute.tsx` L102–111](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/routes/LandingRoute.tsx#L102-L111)).\n     - Pinned permanently in the application header across all authenticated `/agent` routes ([`HeaderBrand.tsx` L17–20](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/components/layout/HeaderBrand.tsx#L17-L20)), watching the cursor across the entire page body (`within=\"body\"`).\n\n---\n\n#### B. Conversational Canvas & Input Mechanics (\"Chat\")\n\n1. **Hark Pro**:\n   - Bottom-docked search and command input bar with speech recognition, file attachment sheets, and dynamic prompt pills.\n   - Inline cloud browser live-view stream embedded in the thread.\n\n2. **Vigil**:\n   - **Floating Input Island ([`InputPill.tsx` L24–120](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/components/chat/InputPill.tsx#L24-L120))**:\n     - Centered floating island (`max-w-2xl`) with auto-expanding textarea (1 to 6 rows, up to 160px), multi-file attachment sheet, and animated state transitions.\n   - **The Handoff Beam ([`handoff-beam.tsx` L361–400](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/components/ui/handoff-beam.tsx#L361-L400))**:\n     - Directly derived from Hark’s Handoff brand identity. Lights a hairline along the composer's bottom edge with a critically damped 2D canvas spring.\n     - Transitions smoothly across 4 phases: `idle` (breathing line), `listening` (crests drawing inward), `thinking` (traveling shimmer), and `speaking` (calm outward ripples).\n     - *Verified Status*: Real-time audio FFT capture is wired to the visualizer, but speech-to-text transcription remains explicitly disconnected ([`InputPill.tsx` L103](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/components/chat/InputPill.tsx#L103)).\n\n---\n\n## 4. Technical Architectural Matrix: Hark Pro vs. Vigil\n\n| Dimension | **Hark Pro** | **Vigil (Open-Source Hark)** |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Foundational Concept** | Commercial \"Operating System for your life\" (SaaS) | Private, self-hosted \"Open-Source Hark\" & digital companion |\n| **Hosting & Tenancy** | Proprietary multi-tenant cloud (`hark.com`) | 100% self-hosted, single-user on private hardware / Docker |\n| **Device Authentication** | SaaS OAuth / SSO / Email magic link | Local cryptographic device pairing (`/pair`) stored in IndexedDB |\n| **Execution Environment** | Hosted Cloud VM cluster (up to 6 parallel browsers) | Local isolated Docker sandbox (`deploy/Dockerfile.sandbox`) |\n| **Execution Observability** | Real-time live browser preview window in chat thread | Expandable [`ThinkingCapsule`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/components/chat/ThinkingCapsule.tsx) step trace & bash terminal |\n| **Deliverables** | In-thread responses or dedicated Project Panels | Decoupled, downloadable [`ArtifactCard`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/components/chat/ArtifactCard.tsx) components |\n| **Proactivity Model** | Cloud poller across third-party consumer SaaS APIs | Two-stage Jev probability gate ($p < 0.3 \\rightarrow$ discard; [`service.py`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/backend/src/modules/triage/service.py)) |\n| **Information Surface** | Dynamic dashboard panels & local weather atmosphere | Morning Briefing Deck (`/agent`) with 3px urgency rails |\n| **Credential Safety** | Proprietary \"Secured by Hark\" Vault | Local environment variables & secrets encryption |\n| **Human-in-the-Loop** | Vault confirmation prompts for transactions | Backend [`ApprovalResponse`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/backend/src/modules/approvals/data.py) *(Frontend route broken)* |\n| **Audio / Voice** | Full cloud speech-to-text and voice prompts | Reactive [`HandoffBeam`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/components/ui/handoff-beam.tsx) visualizer *(STT transcription stubbed)* |\n| **Companion / Pet** | None (deliberately avoided for Apple-grade luxury) | 3D-spherical eye-tracking morphing pet ([`EyeTracker.tsx`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/components/landing/EyeTracker.tsx)) |\n| **Aesthetic Language** | Apple squircle glassmorphism & color accents | Monochromatic ink-on-paper with subtle dawn atmospheric drift |\n| **Motion Engine** | Proprietary smooth Apple UI transitions | Intended CSS `linear()` spring; implemented as `cubic-bezier` |\n\n---\n\n## 5. Architectural Gap Analysis: What Vigil Needs to Truly Match Hark Pro\n\nTo achieve its mission as an **Open-Source Hark**, Vigil has several immediate engineering and UI/UX gaps to close:\n\n1. **Self-Hosted Visual Browser Execution (Open-Source \"Handoff\")**:\n   - Hark Pro’s primary differentiator is the live browser window showing the agent clicking and booking in real-time.\n   - Vigil currently executes headless shell/file commands in Docker. Integrating a containerized browser (e.g. Playwright with WebRTC/noVNC stream) embedded directly into Vigil's `ThinkingCapsule` would deliver Hark's \"Window into the Machine\" in a 100% private, self-hosted setup.\n2. **Repairing the Disconnected Approvals UI**:\n   - The backend approval engine ([`backend/src/modules/approvals/`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/backend/src/modules/approvals/)) is fully functional, but the web client has an unregistered `/agent/approvals` route and an orphaned [`useApprovals()`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/queries/approvals.ts#L9) query.\n   - An approval review sheet or modal must be wired into `/agent` and `/agent/chat` to allow users to approve external mutations.\n3. **Upgrading `HandoffBeam` to Real Bidirectional Voice**:\n   - Currently, the microphone capture only feeds an audio visualizer before informing the user: *\"Transcription is not connected yet\"*.\n   - Integrating a local Whisper model (or Web Speech API fallback) will upgrade Vigil from a visual homage into a functional voice companion.\n4. **Motion Engine Alignment**:\n   - Update [`tokens.css` L18](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/styles/tokens.css#L18) from `cubic-bezier(0.25, 1, 0.5, 1)` to the CSS `linear()` spring curve defined in [`design.md` L326–339](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/design.md#L326-L339) to match physics with React spring components.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Remaining Questions & Gaps\n\n1. **Hark Pro's Cloud Computer-Use Latency & Takeover Protocol**:\n   - Because Hark Pro is proprietary software, the exact frame rates, compression codecs (H.264 vs. WebRTC vs. DOM snapshots), and server-side container recycling latencies used by Handoff cannot be audited from source code.\n2. **Mobile Screen Alignment for the Digital Pet**:\n   - While [`EyeTracker.tsx`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/components/landing/EyeTracker.tsx) responds to touch pointers, speech bubble clipping should be verified on viewports $< 360\\,\\text{px}$ to prevent horizontal overflow when pinned in the top-left margin ([`HeaderBrand.tsx`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/components/layout/HeaderBrand.tsx)).\n3. **Priorities for Next Investigation**:\n   - Implement the missing `/agent/approvals` route in `App.tsx` and design the approval card surface on `/agent`.\n   - Benchmark the feasibility of streaming containerized Playwright screencasts over WebSockets/SSE into Vigil's chat canvas.\n\nThoroughly review the findings above. Carefully check if they fully address every single aspect of the user's question — do not skip any part. Iterate if necessary following the **Workflow** in your system prompt.\n</SYSTEM_MESSAGE>"}
