4:    this. They work, they are tuned, and rewriting the innards\n35:    of two live components to prove a point about duplication\n36:    is how a good afternoon becomes a bad one. This is the one\n37:    new code uses.\n38: \n39:    Frames, not milliseconds. `dt` is expressed in sixtieths of\n40:    a second and the damping is RAISED to it rather than\n41:    multiplied by it, so a dropped frame decays the same amount\n42:    of energy as the two frames it replaced. Multiplying is the\n43:    version that makes a spring behave differently on a busy\n44:    page, which is the hardest kind of bug to see.\n45: \n46:    The loop parks itself the moment the value has settled.\n47:    CLAUDE.md is not complimentary about the one permanent\n48:    requestAnimationFrame already on this bench and there is no\n49:    case for five more. */\n50: "}
