{"step_index":14,"source":"SYSTEM","type":"SYSTEM_MESSAGE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-10T17:31:39Z","content":"The following is a <SYSTEM_MESSAGE> not actually sent by the user. It is provided by the system as important information to pay attention to.\n\n<SYSTEM_MESSAGE>\n[Message] timestamp=2026-11-10T17:31:39Z sender=5e31dc7c-45b3-4353-8d63-a904967edc7e priority=MESSAGE_PRIORITY_HIGH content=DeepInvestigator pipeline completed.\n\n**Investigation Findings**:\n# Architectural & UI/UX Investigation Report: Evolving Vigil into an Open-Source Hark Pro\n\n**To**: Parent Coordinator (`5e31dc7c-45b3-4353-8d63-a904967edc7e`)  \n**From**: Antigravity Technical Investigator  \n**Subject**: Skeptical Codebase Audit & Architectural Blueprint — Transforming Vigil to Mirror Hark Pro's GUI Paradigm, Sandboxed Micro-App Showcases, Third-Party Cloud Browsers (Firecrawl / Browserbase), Groq Whisper STT, Verb-Driven Proactivity, Inline Approvals, Credential Vault, and Dynamic MCP Extensibility\n\n---\n\n## 1. Executive Summary & Strategic Paradigm Shift\n\n**Hark Pro** (launched in October 2026 by Brett Adcock, founder of Figure AI, with industrial design directed by former Apple design lead Abidur Chowdhury) represents an intentional repudiation of the legacy conversational AI paradigm. Hark rejects the blank chat box as an archaic command-line terminal, replacing it with an **ambient Graphical User Interface (GUI) and proactive Operating System for your life**.\n\nIts core architectural and design pillars include:\n1. **Interactive Micro-Apps & Panels**: Dynamically building small, interactive single-purpose websites, widgets, and mini-dashboards from user prompts and live account signals.\n2. **Autonomous Cloud Computer (\"Handoff\")**: Running headless multi-session browsers in the cloud, paired with an optional live execution viewing window where users can watch the agent browse, click, type, and complete digital chores.\n3. **Proactivity Tags & Verb-Based Action Buttons**: Eliminating passive notifications and generic CRUD labels (\"Submit\", \"Run\", \"Dismiss\") in favor of natural-language observation tags paired with explicit active verbs (`[ Draft ]`, `[ Book ]`, `[ Pay ]`, `[ RSVP ]`, `[ Cancel ]`, `[ Reschedule ]`).\n4. **Human-in-the-Loop Approvals**: Frictionless, inline decision cards that pause high-stakes actions (payments, outbound messages, bookings) for single-tap user authorization.\n5. **Calm, Apple-Caliber Tactile Aesthetic**: Deep obsidian and warm ivory tones, continuous squircle geometry, refined vector iconography, and the complete absence of cartoon mascots, neon gradients, or generic AI confetti.\n6. **Encrypted Credential Vault (\"Secured by Hark\")**: Enterprise-grade credential management isolating sensitive third-party passwords, cookies, and API keys.\n\n### Vigil's Strategic Adaptation Path\nRather than requiring self-hosters to spin up a resource-draining, crash-prone local VM farm of headless Chromium browsers and long-running Docker web servers, Vigil can achieve **full feature parity as an open-source Hark Pro** through an adapted architecture:\n- **Sandbox Micro-App Showcase**: Upgrading Vigil's Docker sandbox and frontend artifact pipeline to build, bundle, and showcase interactive client-side SPAs and static web apps in secure, responsive sandboxed iframes (`sandbox=\"allow-scripts allow-forms\"`), pinnable directly onto the dashboard as live home screen Panels.\n- **Third-Party Online Browser API (Firecrawl / Browserbase)**: Replacing local browser VM overhead with an API-driven cloud browser service using `FIRECRAWL_API_KEY` (for structured extraction, markdown conversion, and DOM action sequences) and optional Browserbase live debugger URLs (for live visual execution windows).\n- **Sub-250ms Voice STT via Groq Whisper**: Wiring frontend `MediaRecorder` audio capture to Groq's `whisper-large-v3-turbo` API via a new dedicated backend voice endpoint, populating the input draft seamlessly.\n- **Decommissioning the Mascot**: Removing `<EyeTracker />` from [`HeaderBrand.tsx`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/components/layout/HeaderBrand.tsx#L18) and [`LandingRoute.tsx`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/routes/LandingRoute.tsx#L102), adopting a minimalist `Vigil ✦` brand mark.\n- **Verb-Driven Proactivity & Inline Approvals**: Restructuring the triage pipeline and card schemas to generate natural-language proactivity tags and active verb triggers; repairing Vigil's broken approvals navigation by deploying first-class inline approval decision cards in chat and home feeds.\n- **Encrypted Credential Vault & Dynamic MCP Integration**: Surfacing an AES-256-GCM credential vault in Settings for API keys/logins, and resolving Vigil's critical defect where discovered MCP tools were never injected into the LLM's tool schemas.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Challenging the Prior Investigation: Audit, Evidence & Corrections\n\nA critical audit of the prior attempt reveals several verified findings alongside **major logical leaps, lifecycle misconceptions, and missing code paths**:\n\n### 2.1 The Container Teardown Fallacy (Strategy B Critique)\n- **Prior Claim**: The prior investigator proposed hosting complex multi-file dev servers (e.g. Vite on port 5173) inside the Docker sandbox by adding `network: \"bridge\"` and reverse-proxying `GET /api/v1/sandbox/preview/{run_id}/{path:path}` from FastAPI to the running container's internal IP.\n- **Evidence in Code**:\n  - In [`backend/src/worker.py:127-131`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/backend/src/worker.py#L127-L131) and [`backend/src/worker.py:153-157`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/backend/src/worker.py#L153-L157):\n    ```python\n    try:\n        await service.process(run_id, observer=context.observer)\n    finally:\n        await executor.close()\n    ```\n  - In [`backend/src/dependencies.py:734-749`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/backend/src/dependencies.py#L734-L749):\n    ```python\n    async def close(self) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Snapshot /workspace and remove the run container.\"\"\"\n        ...\n        await self.sandbox.stop_and_remove(container_id)\n    ```\n  - In [`backend/src/modules/runs/tools/shell.py:59-65`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/backend/src/modules/runs/tools/shell.py#L59-L65): `bash` executes `stream_exec` with a synchronous timeout; any foreground dev server blocks the tool until timeout, causing process termination.\n- **Corrected Finding**: The prior investigator completely missed that **Vigil's container lifecycle is strictly ephemeral: containers are immediately stopped and deleted (`stop_and_remove`) the moment a run step finishes**. A reverse proxy to a container IP will fail with `ConnectionRefused` or `HostUnreachable`.\n- **The Correct Solution**:\n  1. **Self-Contained Dynamic Panels (Single-Page Apps)**: For single-file HTML/CSS/JS (with embedded Tailwind, React, Lucide, Canvas, or ECharts), render directly via `srcDoc` in a sandboxed iframe. This is instantaneous, zero-cost, persistent, and survives container teardown.\n  2. **Static Hosted Bundles (Multi-File Web Projects)**: For Vite/React/static web projects built in Docker, have the agent output to `/workspace/dist`, package the directory into the host delivery directory as a `web_bundle` artifact, and serve it via a static asset endpoint:\n     `GET /api/v1/artifacts/{artifact_id}/site/{filepath:path}`\n     This hosts the built website permanently on the backend host with strict sandboxed Content-Security-Policy headers, with zero background container overhead.\n\n### 2.2 The Broken Approvals Disconnect in the Web Client\n- **Prior Claim**: The prior investigator noted that `/agent/approvals` was missing from `App.tsx`.\n- **Deeper Investigation into the Disconnect**:\n  - In [`web/src/routes/ChatRoute.tsx:92-98`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/routes/ChatRoute.tsx#L92-L98):\n    ```tsx\n    <button onClick={() => navigate('/agent/approvals')}>\n      The agent is waiting on your approval, open Approvals to decide\n    </button>\n    ```\n  - In [`web/src/App.tsx:95-107`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/App.tsx#L95-L107): The router defines only `/agent`, `/agent/chat`, and `/agent/settings`. Any other route hits the catch-all `*` and redirects to `/agent`.\n  - In [`web/src/components/home/TaskCard.tsx:115-119`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/components/home/TaskCard.tsx#L115-L119):\n    ```tsx\n    const isKnown = (action: CardAction) =>\n      (action.action_type === 'run' && ...) ||\n      action.action_type === 'dismiss' ||\n      action.action_type === 'reply';\n    ```\n    If `card.status === 'awaiting_approval'`, action buttons are marked unknown and **disabled** (`disabled={busy || !isKnown(primary)}` at L200).\n  - In [`web/src/components/chat/ThinkingCapsule.tsx:996-1002`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/components/chat/ThinkingCapsule.tsx#L996-L1002):\n    ```tsx\n    if (item.kind === 'approval_required') {\n      return (\n        <div className=\"flex items-center gap-2 rounded-[10px] border border-amber-500/25 bg-amber-500/8 px-3 py-2 text-[12px] text-amber-200\">\n          <span>Waiting on your approval to execute external action</span>\n        </div>\n      );\n    }\n    ```\n  - In [`web/src/queries/approvals.ts:29-49`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/queries/approvals.ts#L29-L49): `useDecideApproval` and `api.decideApproval` are implemented, but **not a single React component in the entire frontend ever invokes them**.\n- **Corrected Finding**: Vigil's approvals system is completely paralyzed at the UI layer. The backend approval machinery ([`backend/src/modules/approvals/service.py:1-100`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/backend/src/modules/approvals/service.py#L1-L100)) is fully functional, but the frontend provides zero functional interaction. Hark Pro solves this by embedding **inline approval decision checkpoints** directly into the conversation stream and on the card itself.\n\n### 2.3 The Triage Hardcoding Defect\n- **Prior Claim**: Cards have generic action types.\n- **Deeper Investigation into Triage**:\n  - In [`backend/src/modules/triage/service.py:127-130`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/backend/src/modules/triage/service.py#L127-L130):\n    ```python\n    actions = [\n        CardActionDTO(id=\"quick_reply\", label=\"Quick Reply\", action_type=\"reply\", payload={\"thread_id\": thread_id}),\n        CardActionDTO(id=\"mark_done\", label=\"Mark Done\", action_type=\"dismiss\", payload={}),\n    ]\n    ```\n  - Every card synthesized by the triage worker is hardcoded to \"Quick Reply\" and \"Mark Done\".\n- **Corrected Finding**: Triage never emits dynamic, verb-based actions. To mirror Hark Pro, the triage prompt/classifier must synthesize both a **proactivity tag** (contextual observation) and an **action verb** (`Draft`, `Book`, `Pay`, `RSVP`).\n\n### 2.4 The MCP Tool Exposure Black Hole\n- **Verified Prior Claim**:\n  - In [`backend/src/modules/runs/service.py:522-527`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/backend/src/modules/runs/service.py#L522-L527):\n    ```python\n    config = await self.journal.get_config(run.config_id)\n    declared = list(config.tools) if config is not None else []\n    loop = self.build_loop(\n        observer=observer,\n        tool_schemas=openai_tool_declarations(declared),\n    )\n    ```\n  - In [`backend/src/modules/runs/tools/__init__.py:220-238`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/backend/src/modules/runs/tools/__init__.py#L220-L238): `openai_tool_declarations` iterates strictly over `src.modules.runs.tools.TOOLS` (the 12 built-in tools). Any external tool name is discarded.\n- **Corrected Finding**: Discovered MCP tools from connected servers are stored in the database but are completely invisible to the LLM model. A dynamic schema injection hook is necessary in `RunsService.build_loop()`.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Detailed Architectural Blueprint: Mirroring Hark Pro\n\n```\n┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                                   VIGIL / HARK PRO ARCHITECTURE                        │\n└────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n                                           │\n         ┌─────────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────┐\n         ▼                                 ▼                                ▼\n┌─────────────────┐             ┌─────────────────────┐          ┌──────────────────────┐\n│   VOICE INPUT   │             │   MICRO-APP SHOWCASE│          │  THIRD-PARTY BROWSER │\n│  (Groq Whisper) │             │ (Panels / Sandboxes)│          │ (Firecrawl / B-base) │\n└─────────────────┘             └─────────────────────┘          └──────────────────────┘\n  • MediaRecorder (WebM/Opus)     • Single-File SPAs (srcDoc)      • Firecrawl Scrape API\n  • POST /voice/transcribe        • Multi-File Bundles (Host CDN)  • Actions: Click/Type/DOM\n  • whisper-large-v3-turbo        • Isolated iframe (no same-org)  • Schema JSON Extraction\n  • Sub-250ms draft insert        • Pinned Dashboard Panels        • Optional Live Debug View\n         │                                 │                                │\n         └─────────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────┘\n                                           │\n         ┌─────────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────┐\n         ▼                                 ▼                                ▼\n┌─────────────────┐             ┌─────────────────────┐          ┌──────────────────────┐\n│  PROACTIVITY &  │             │   HUMAN APPROVALS   │          │  ENCRYPTED VAULT &   │\n│  VERB BUTTONS   │             │ (Inline Checkpoints)│          │     DYNAMIC MCP      │\n└─────────────────┘             └─────────────────────┘          └──────────────────────┘\n  • \"Michael wants to email\"      • Inline chat approval cards     • AES-256-GCM Vault\n  • Verb triggers: [Draft],[Book] • Exact params & diff preview    • Connectors UI in Settings\n  • Direct seed execution         • One-tap Decide: POST /decision • Dynamic schema injection\n  • Home feed action dispatch     • Loop resumes instantly (202)   • External partition gate\n```\n\n---\n\n### 3.1 Mirroring the VM Farm: Micro-App & Small Website Showcase\n\nHark Pro's signature capability is generating interactive mini-apps, calculators, dashboards, and single-purpose utilities on the fly and showcasing them directly to users.\n\n#### 1. Current Vigil Defect\nIn [`web/src/components/chat/ArtifactCard.tsx:504-508`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/components/chat/ArtifactCard.tsx#L504-L508) and [`L672-676`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/components/chat/ArtifactCard.tsx#L672-L676), HTML deliverables are rendered inside a `<pre>` tag as raw text:\n```tsx\n<pre className=\"whitespace-pre-wrap font-mono text-[12.5px] leading-[1.65] text-[var(--text)]\">\n  {fullText ?? item.preview ?? 'Document ready for download.'}\n</pre>\n```\nJavaScript is never executed, stylesheets are ignored, and no interactive UI appears.\n\n#### 2. Dual Showcase Architecture\nTo provide full micro-app capabilities without requiring a running Docker container after the run ends:\n\n##### Tier 1: Single-Page Dynamic Micro-Apps & Panels (`srcDoc` Sandboxing)\n- **Use Case**: Calculators, financial planners, live charts, data tables, SVG visualizers, lightweight games, and prompt-generated dashboards.\n- **Agent Generation**: The agent uses `generate_document(filename=\"mortgage_calc\", content=\"...\", format=\"html\")` or writes `index.html` via `write`.\n- **Interactive Webview Component**: Render an isolated iframe in `ArtifactCard.tsx` and a new `PanelCard.tsx`:\n  ```tsx\n  <iframe\n    sandbox=\"allow-scripts allow-forms\"\n    srcDoc={sanitizedHtml}\n    title={item.name}\n    className=\"w-full h-[520px] rounded-[16px] border border-[var(--border)] bg-white shadow-inner\"\n  />\n  ```\n- **Security Guarantee**: Omitting `allow-same-origin` ensures that scripts executed inside the micro-app cannot access parent `window`, `localStorage` (containing device auth tokens), cookies, or IndexedDB.\n- **Controls**: Viewport switcher: **Mobile (375px)** | **Tablet (768px)** | **Desktop (100%)**, plus pop-out in a new browser tab.\n- **Dashboard Pinning (\"Add to Home Panels\")**: Users can click a \"Pin to Home\" button on any micro-app artifact, saving it to `WidgetsRail.tsx` as a permanent live Panel on their home screen.\n\n##### Tier 2: Static Multi-File Hosted Apps (`web_bundle` Artifacts)\n- **Use Case**: React/Vite/Tailwind multi-file apps, multi-page docs, web applications with separate CSS/JS/images.\n- **Build Execution**: The agent builds the project in `/workspace` using `bash` (`npm run build`). Output lands in `/workspace/dist`.\n- **Bundle Packaging**: A new delivery tool `deliver_site(directory=\"/workspace/dist\", name=\"app\")` archives the build directory to the host delivery path and records an artifact of kind `web_app`.\n- **Backend Asset Hosting**: Add route in [`backend/src/modules/artifacts/router.py`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/backend/src/modules/artifacts/router.py):\n  `GET /api/v1/artifacts/{artifact_id}/site/{filepath:path}`\n  FastAPI serves static files with headers:\n  `Content-Security-Policy: sandbox allow-scripts allow-forms; default-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' data: blob:; connect-src *`\n- **Zero Running Container Needed**: The site is hosted statically from host disk; no Docker container remains running.\n\n---\n\n### 3.2 Third-Party Online Browser Integration (Firecrawl / Browserbase)\n\nRather than maintaining a heavy, local VM farm running headless Chromium sessions that consume gigabytes of host RAM and trigger anti-bot bans, Vigil connects to third-party cloud browser APIs.\n\n#### 1. Current Web Tool Limitations\nIn [`backend/src/modules/runs/tools/search.py:23-98`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/backend/src/modules/runs/tools/search.py#L23-L98), Vigil only exposes `web_search_exa` and `web_fetch_exa`. The agent cannot interact with web applications, click buttons, fill forms, or navigate SPAs.\n\n#### 2. Cloud Browser Tool Suite\nImplement three core browser tools in `backend/src/modules/runs/tools/browser.py`:\n\n```python\nclass BrowserNavigateArgs(BaseModel):\n    url: str = Field(..., description=\"Target web URL to navigate to\")\n    actions: list[dict[str, Any]] = Field(\n        default_factory=list,\n        description=\"Sequential browser actions: click, write, wait, press, scroll, screenshot\"\n    )\n\nclass BrowserExtractArgs(BaseModel):\n    url: str = Field(..., description=\"Target web page URL\")\n    prompt: str = Field(..., description=\"Extraction goal description\")\n    schema_definition: dict[str, Any] = Field(..., description=\"JSON Schema of required output\")\n```\n\n1. **`browser_navigate`**:\n   - Dispatches to Firecrawl API (`POST https://api.firecrawl.dev/v1/scrape`) with `formats: [\"markdown\", \"screenshot\"]`.\n   - Executes interactive sequences:\n     ```json\n     [\n       {\"type\": \"write\", \"text\": \"flight from SFO to JFK\", \"selector\": \"input[name='q']\"},\n       {\"type\": \"press\", \"key\": \"Enter\"},\n       {\"type\": \"wait\", \"milliseconds\": 2000},\n       {\"type\": \"screenshot\"}\n     ]\n     ```\n   - Returns structured page markdown and a screenshot image URL.\n2. **`browser_extract`**:\n   - Leverages Firecrawl's LLM extraction to return validated JSON matching the requested schema.\n3. **Live \"Handoff\" Window (Browserbase / Steel Integration)**:\n   - When a task requires continuous visual feedback, the tool provisions a session via Browserbase (`https://api.browserbase.com/v1/sessions`).\n   - Browserbase returns a `session.liveUrl` (an interactive remote debugging stream).\n   - Vigil's frontend renders an inline live stream iframe directly in the chat message stream, allowing the user to watch the cursor navigate, type, and click in real time.\n\n---\n\n### 3.3 Ultra-Fast Voice Input via Groq Whisper STT\n\n#### 1. Current Frontend Stub\nIn [`web/src/components/chat/InputPill.tsx:81-94`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/components/chat/InputPill.tsx#L81-L94), audio capture connects to an `AnalyserNode` for waveform visualization, but line 103 simply prints:\n`'Microphone stopped. Transcription is not connected yet.'`\nNo audio data is saved or transmitted.\n\n#### 2. End-to-End Groq Pipeline\n1. **Frontend Capture (`InputPill.tsx`)**:\n   - On `startCapture`, instantiate `MediaRecorder(stream, { mimeType: 'audio/webm;codecs=opus' })` (falling back to `'audio/mp4'` on iOS Safari).\n   - Collect audio buffers on `ondataavailable`.\n   - On `stopCapture`, assemble `const blob = new Blob(chunks, { type: 'audio/webm' })`.\n   - Upload via `POST /api/v1/voice/transcribe` as multipart form data.\n   - Insert transcription into `draft` state (`setDraft((prev) => (prev ? `${prev} ${text}` : text))`) so the user can inspect or edit before submission.\n2. **Backend Router (`backend/src/modules/voice/router.py`)**:\n   - Add `voice` to `MODULE_FACTORIES` in [`backend/src/config/router.py:24-41`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/backend/src/config/router.py#L24-L41).\n   - Proxy the audio payload to Groq's Audio API (`https://api.groq.com/openai/v1/audio/transcriptions`):\n     ```python\n     @router.post(\"/transcribe\", response_model=VoiceTranscribeResponse)\n     async def transcribe_audio(\n         file: UploadFile = File(...),\n         settings: Settings = Depends(get_settings),\n         _device: DeviceDTO = Depends(get_current_device),\n     ) -> VoiceTranscribeResponse:\n         api_key = settings.GROQ_API_KEY\n         if not api_key:\n             raise ValidationError(\"Groq API key is not configured in settings or vault\")\n         async with httpx.AsyncClient(timeout=30.0) as client:\n             res = await client.post(\n                 \"https://api.groq.com/openai/v1/audio/transcriptions\",\n                 headers={\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {api_key}\"},\n                 files={\"file\": (file.filename or \"audio.webm\", await file.read(), file.content_type)},\n                 data={\"model\": \"whisper-large-v3-turbo\", \"response_format\": \"json\"},\n             )\n             res.raise_for_status()\n             return VoiceTranscribeResponse(text=res.json()[\"text\"])\n     ```\n   - Latency for a 5-second audio snippet is typically **120ms to 220ms**, enabling instant voice-to-text.\n\n---\n\n### 3.4 Mascot Removal & Apple-Inspired Design Language\n\n#### 1. Decommissioning `<EyeTracker />`\n- **Brand Lockup**: In [`web/src/components/layout/HeaderBrand.tsx:16-20`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/components/layout/HeaderBrand.tsx#L16-L20), remove `<EyeTracker />`. Replace with a clean typographic mark: `Vigil` followed by a subtle geometric vector spark `✦` featuring an ambient breathing opacity pulse.\n- **Landing Page**: In [`web/src/routes/LandingRoute.tsx:23, 102`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/routes/LandingRoute.tsx#L23), remove the eye-tracker import and instance. In the hero section, replace the mascot container with an interactive preview card showcasing Hark-style proactivity cards and a live micro-app panel.\n\n#### 2. Hark Pro Design Philosophy (Abidur Chowdhury Aesthetic)\n- **Atmospheric Palette**: Deep obsidian-to-midnight-navy (`#070A10` to `#0A0F1D`) in dark mode; tactile ivory/cream (`#FBF9F5` / `#FFFFFF`) in light mode.\n- **Squircle Ergonomics**: Organic continuous curvature (`rounded-[20px]` to `rounded-[28px]` on containers, `rounded-full` on pills and docks).\n- **Tactile Materiality**: Subdued borders (`rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08)`), micro-blur backdrops (`backdrop-blur-md`), and specular top-edge rim highlights.\n- **Zero AI Clutter**: Prohibit emoji icons in UI navigation; enforce clean, thin-stroke `lucide-react` vector glyphs (`strokeWidth={1.5}`).\n\n---\n\n### 3.5 Proactivity Tags & Verb-Based Action Buttons\n\n#### 1. The Interaction Model\nIn Hark Pro, tasks are framed around what the AI observed (proactivity tag) and what specific action it proposes to take (verb button):\n\n| Hark Pro Proactivity Tag | Context / Observation | Primary Verb Button | Secondary Action |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `✦ Michael wants to book an email` | Email received asking for Q4 numbers | **[ Draft ]** | `[ Dismiss ]` |\n| `✦ Flight confirmed: SFO → JFK` | Flight booked, no hotel reservation found | **[ Find Hotels ]** | `[ Ignore ]` |\n| `✦ Stripe invoice due tomorrow ($120)` | SaaS subscription renewal reminder | **[ Pay ]** | `[ Review Details ]` |\n| `✦ Overlapping calendar invitations` | Team sync conflicts with executive review | **[ Reschedule ]** | `[ Decline Sync ]` |\n| `✦ Figma team seats inactive (3 seats)` | Unused seats costing $45/mo | **[ Cancel Seats ]** | `[ Keep ]` |\n\n#### 2. Codebase Schema Extensions\n1. In [`backend/src/modules/cards/data.py:8-16`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/backend/src/modules/cards/data.py#L8-L16):\n   ```python\n   class CardActionSchema(BaseModel):\n       id: str\n       label: str = Field(..., description=\"Verb or label (e.g. 'Draft', 'Book')\")\n       verb: str = Field(..., description=\"Explicit action verb ('draft', 'book', 'pay', 'rsvp')\")\n       action_type: str = Field(..., description=\"'verb_action', 'run', 'approval', 'dismiss', 'reply'\")\n       payload: dict[str, Any] = Field(default_factory=dict)\n   ```\n2. In `CardResponse`: Add `proactivity_tag: str | None = None` (e.g., `\"Michael wants to book an email\"`).\n3. In [`backend/src/modules/triage/service.py:127-143`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/backend/src/modules/triage/service.py#L127-L143): Update stage 2 synthesis to analyze incoming item intent and generate appropriate proactivity tags and action verbs.\n4. In [`web/src/components/home/TaskCard.tsx:95-125`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/components/home/TaskCard.tsx#L95-L125):\n   - Render the `proactivity_tag` at the top of the card with a `✦` accent mark.\n   - When the primary verb button (e.g. `[ Draft ]`) is clicked, dispatch a run initialized with that explicit intent or navigate to chat with the pre-seeded workflow.\n\n---\n\n### 3.6 Human-in-the-Loop Inline Approvals System\n\n#### 1. The Broken Navigation Fix\n- Remove the dead link to `/agent/approvals` in [`web/src/routes/ChatRoute.tsx:94`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/routes/ChatRoute.tsx#L94).\n- Transform approvals into **first-class inline cards embedded directly in the message stream**.\n\n#### 2. Inline Approval Decision Card\nWhen a run step emits `event_type: \"approval_required\"` (with `approval_id` in payload):\n1. In [`web/src/components/chat/ThinkingCapsule.tsx:996-1002`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/components/chat/ThinkingCapsule.tsx#L996-L1002) and [`web/src/components/chat/MessageStream.tsx`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/components/chat/MessageStream.tsx), fetch or receive the approval details.\n2. Render an **Approval Decision Card**:\n   - **Target Action**: e.g., `Send Email`, `Browser Purchase`, `Stripe Payment`, or `Delete File`.\n   - **Parameter Diff**: Recipient address, message subject, order summary, or dollar amount.\n   - **Action Buttons**:\n     - Primary Button: Active verb: e.g., **`[ Approve & Send ]`** or **`[ Authorize $45.00 ]`**.\n     - Secondary Button: **`[ Reject ]`** or **`[ Edit Parameters ]`**.\n3. Clicking Approve calls `api.decideApproval(approvalId, { decision: 'approved' })`.\n4. The backend records the decision, enqueues `resume_run` ([`backend/src/modules/approvals/service.py:5-6`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/backend/src/modules/approvals/service.py#L5-L6)), the loop transitions from `awaiting_approval` back to `running`, and execution proceeds without page refreshes.\n\n---\n\n### 3.7 Account Support & \"Secured by Hark\" Credential Vault\n\n#### 1. Vault Storage Architecture\nVigil already contains robust AES-256-GCM encryption primitives in [`backend/src/config/security.py:87-120`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/backend/src/config/security.py#L87-L120) (`encrypt_secret`, `decrypt_secret`) and database models for `connected_accounts` in [`backend/src/schemas/connectors.py:30-85`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/backend/src/schemas/connectors.py#L30-L85).\n\n#### 2. User-Facing Implementation\n1. **Settings > Connectors & Vault UI**:\n   - Replace the empty placeholder in [`web/src/components/settings/sections.tsx:266-326`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/components/settings/sections.tsx#L266-L326) with an interactive **Vault Management Center**.\n   - Categories:\n     - **AI Services**: Groq API Key (Voice STT), Firecrawl API Key (Web Browser), OpenAI/Anthropic Keys.\n     - **Connected Services**: Google Workspace (Gmail/Calendar OAuth), Slack, GitHub.\n2. **Encrypted Persistence**:\n   - `POST /api/v1/connectors/accounts` encrypts submitted credentials via `encrypt_secret(payload.secret, settings.SECRET_KEY)` before writing to `connected_accounts.encrypted_credentials`.\n3. **Runtime Tool Decryption**:\n   - When tools (`browser_navigate`, `voice_transcribe`, or email tools) execute, the tool context fetches and decrypts the credentials in memory for the duration of the request.\n\n---\n\n### 3.8 Dynamic MCP (Model Context Protocol) Connection Engine\n\n#### 1. Resolving the Tool Exposure Defect\nIn [`backend/src/modules/runs/service.py:522-527`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/backend/src/modules/runs/service.py#L522-L527):\n```python\n# CURRENT FLAW:\ndeclared = list(config.tools) if config is not None else []\nloop = self.build_loop(\n    observer=observer,\n    tool_schemas=openai_tool_declarations(declared),  # Only inspects static TOOLS!\n)\n```\n**Fix**:\n1. Query discovered tools from `ConnectorsService.list_mcp_tools()`.\n2. Map each `MCPDiscoveredToolDTO` into the standard OpenAI function tool schema:\n   ```python\n   mcp_schemas = [\n       {\n           \"type\": \"function\",\n           \"function\": {\n               \"name\": tool.name,\n               \"description\": tool.description,\n               \"parameters\": tool.input_schema,\n           },\n       }\n       for tool in active_mcp_tools\n   ]\n   all_schemas = [*openai_tool_declarations(declared), *mcp_schemas]\n   ```\n3. Pass `all_schemas` into `build_loop(tool_schemas=all_schemas)`.\n4. In `PartitionPolicy` ([`backend/src/modules/runs/state.py:270-318`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/backend/src/modules/runs/state.py#L270-L318)), assign discovered MCP tools to the `\"external\"` partition by default, guaranteeing that any third-party MCP action triggers an **inline approval card** before execution.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Architectural Comparison Matrix\n\n| Dimension | Hark Pro | Current Vigil Implementation | Adapted Vigil Architecture (Open-Source Hark Pro) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **Micro-Apps / Panels** | Cloud VM farm; creates dynamic full-screen widgets & panels | Rendered as monospace text `<pre>` in `ArtifactCard.tsx:505`; containers killed on exit | Sandboxed iframe preview (`allow-scripts allow-forms`), viewport toggles, static hosted asset bundles (`/artifacts/{id}/site/...`), dashboard home pinning |\n| **Web Browser** | Proprietary \"Handoff\" cloud browser computer | Exa semantic search/fetch only (`search.py`); zero browser automation | Firecrawl API (actions: `click`, `write`, `screenshot`) with `FIRECRAWL_API_KEY`; Browserbase for live visual execution window |\n| **Voice STT** | Native voice mode / speech-to-text across iOS/Android/Web | Audio capture stub in `InputPill.tsx:103` (`Transcription is not connected yet`); no backend route | `MediaRecorder` + Groq Whisper API (`whisper-large-v3-turbo`) via `POST /api/v1/voice/transcribe` (<250ms latency) |\n| **Brand & Aesthetic** | Abidur Chowdhury Apple-inspired tactile design; no mascot | Cube eye-tracker mascot (`EyeTracker.tsx`); ambient dark/light themes | Remove `<EyeTracker />`, minimalist `Vigil ✦` typography mark, warm tactile cream & obsidian palettes |\n| **Proactivity & Verbs** | Natural language observation tags; explicit verb buttons (`Draft`, `Book`, `Pay`) | Hardcoded \"Quick Reply\" / \"Mark Done\" in `triage/service.py:128`; generic `action_type` | Dynamic proactivity tags, explicit verb triggers (`[ Draft ]`, `[ RSVP ]`, `[ Pay ]`), open cards |\n| **Approvals Flow** | Frictionless inline decision checkpoints | `/agent/approvals` link is broken (404/redirect); `ThinkingCapsule` text-only; zero frontend calls to `decideApproval` | First-class inline approval cards in chat stream and home feed with verb confirmations and instant run resumption |\n| **Account Vault** | \"Secured by Hark\" encrypted vault for user logins, cards, and accounts | Schema exists (`connected_accounts`), AES-256-GCM in `security.py`, but zero UI to add keys | Encrypted Credential Vault in Settings > Connectors; dynamic key resolution for tools |\n| **MCP Extensibility** | Native integration with web services | MCP integration layer exists in backend, but discovered tools are NEVER passed to LLM | Dynamic MCP tool schema injection into `RunLoop`; Settings UI for adding MCP servers; inline approval gating |\n\n---\n\n## 5. Remaining Questions & Gaps\n\n1. **Firecrawl vs Browserbase for Real-Time Visual Streaming (\"Handoff\")**:\n   - Firecrawl handles scraping, form filling, and screenshots via stateless REST calls. It does not provide an interactive WebSocket/VNC live video stream.\n   - If the user requires a real-time, 60fps interactive visual window where they can watch the agent cursor move and intervene manually (mirroring Hark's \"Handoff\"), **Browserbase** or **Steel.dev** must be wired as an alternative browser provider alongside Firecrawl.\n   - *Follow-up focus*: Confirm whether visual live streaming is a priority for Phase 1, or if Firecrawl's action sequences and screenshot diffs suffice.\n\n2. **Docker Network Access During Sandbox App Builds**:\n   - If an agent is tasked with building a web app using Node.js/Vite inside the Docker sandbox, running `npm create` or `npm install` requires outbound network access during the build phase.\n   - Currently, `backend/src/integrations/sandbox/contract.py:176, 254` strictly locks containers to `network: \"none\"`.\n   - *Follow-up focus*: Determine the security boundary for build containers: should a restricted bridge network (`network: \"bridge\"`) be permitted specifically for package installation commands, or should common web templates (React, Tailwind, Lucide) be pre-installed inside the sandbox base image?\n\n3. **Multi-User Authentication vs Enhanced Single-Tenant Vault**:\n   - Vigil currently uses single-tenant pairing via an ASCII QR code ([`backend/src/main.py:59-72`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/backend/src/main.py#L59-L72)) mapping to a default user.\n   - *Follow-up focus*: Should connected accounts and credential vaults remain scoped to the paired local device, or is multi-user account authentication (email/password, sessions) required for future hosted deployments?\n\nThoroughly review the findings above. Carefully check if they fully address every single aspect of the user's question — do not skip any part. Iterate if necessary following the **Workflow** in your system prompt.\n</SYSTEM_MESSAGE>"}
{"step_index":15,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-10T17:31:39Z","input_tokens":59929,"cache_read_tokens":0,"output_tokens":6894,"content":"# Architectural & UI/UX Blueprint: Transforming Vigil into an Open-Source Hark Pro\n\n---\n\n## 1. Executive Summary & Strategic Architectural Pivot\n\n**Hark Pro** (designed under the direction of former Apple design lead Abidur Chowdhury, who unveiled the iPhone Air) is architected around a fundamental premise: **the blank chat box is the archaic command-line terminal of AI**. Hark replaces it with an **ambient Graphical User Interface (GUI) and operating system for daily life**.\n\nIts defining user experience rests on six pillars:\n1. **Interactive Micro-Apps & Panels**: Generating single-purpose utilities, interactive dashboards, calculators, and mini-sites on the fly and embedding them directly into the canvas or pinning them as home screen widgets.\n2. **Autonomous Cloud Computer (\"Handoff\")**: Using cloud-hosted browser automation to execute digital errands (booking, form submission, research) with real-time visual proof.\n3. **Proactivity Tags & Verb-Based Action Triggers**: Replacing passive notifications with natural-language observations (`✦ Michael wants to book an email`) paired with single-tap active verb buttons (`[ Draft ]`, `[ Book ]`, `[ Pay ]`, `[ Reschedule ]`).\n4. **Frictionless Inline Approvals**: High-stakes operations (finances, outbound communications, data mutations) pause at inline decision checkpoints directly inside the conversation stream.\n5. **Tactile Apple-Grade Aesthetic**: Warm ivory/cream and deep obsidian tones, squircle geometry, zero cartoon mascots, zero neon gradients, and zero AI clutter.\n6. **Encrypted Credential Vault (\"Secured by Hark\")**: Enterprise-grade credential management isolating passwords, session cookies, and API keys.\n\n### Vigil's Strategic Adaptation Path\nTo mirror Hark Pro without forcing self-hosters to operate an expensive, fragile local VM farm of headless Chromium browsers and long-running Docker web servers, Vigil adapts its architecture as follows:\n\n```\n┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                                   VIGIL / HARK PRO ARCHITECTURE                        │\n└────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n                                           │\n         ┌─────────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────┐\n         ▼                                 ▼                                ▼\n┌─────────────────┐             ┌─────────────────────┐          ┌──────────────────────┐\n│   VOICE INPUT   │             │   MICRO-APP SHOWCASE│          │  THIRD-PARTY BROWSER │\n│  (Groq Whisper) │             │ (Panels / Sandboxes)│          │ (Firecrawl / B-base) │\n└─────────────────┘             └─────────────────────┘          └──────────────────────┘\n  • MediaRecorder (WebM/Opus)     • Single-File SPAs (srcDoc)      • Firecrawl Scrape API\n  • POST /voice/transcribe        • Multi-File Bundles (Host CDN)  • Actions: Click/Type/DOM\n  • whisper-large-v3-turbo        • Isolated iframe (no same-org)  • Schema JSON Extraction\n  • Sub-250ms draft insert        • Pinned Dashboard Panels        • Optional Live Debug View\n         │                                 │                                │\n         └─────────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────┘\n                                           │\n         ┌─────────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────┐\n         ▼                                 ▼                                ▼\n┌─────────────────┐             ┌─────────────────────┐          ┌──────────────────────┐\n│  PROACTIVITY &  │             │   HUMAN APPROVALS   │          │  ENCRYPTED VAULT &   │\n│  VERB BUTTONS   │             │ (Inline Checkpoints)│          │     DYNAMIC MCP      │\n└─────────────────┘             └─────────────────────┘          └──────────────────────┘\n  • \"Michael wants to email\"      • Inline chat approval cards     • AES-256-GCM Vault\n  • Verb triggers: [Draft],[Book] • Exact params & diff preview    • Connectors UI in Settings\n  • Direct seed execution         • One-tap Decide: POST /decision • Dynamic schema injection\n  • Home feed action dispatch     • Loop resumes instantly (202)   • External partition gate\n```\n\n---\n\n## 2. Micro-App & Small Website Showcase (Mirroring the VM Farm)\n\n### Current Flaw in Vigil\nIn [`ArtifactCard.tsx`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/components/chat/ArtifactCard.tsx#L504-L508), HTML deliverables are rendered inside a `<pre>` block as raw text:\n```tsx\n<pre className=\"whitespace-pre-wrap font-mono text-[12.5px] leading-[1.65] text-[var(--text)]\">\n  {fullText ?? item.preview ?? 'Document ready for download.'}\n</pre>\n```\nJavaScript is never executed, styles are ignored, and no interactive UI appears. Furthermore, Vigil's Docker containers are **strictly ephemeral**—the container is destroyed the moment the run loop finishes ([`dependencies.py`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/backend/src/dependencies.py#L734-L749)), meaning reverse-proxying to a long-running container port is impossible.\n\n### Dual-Tier Showcase Solution\n\n#### Tier 1: Single-File Dynamic Micro-Apps & Panels (`srcDoc` Sandboxing)\n- **Use Case**: Interactive calculators, financial planners, live charts, data tables, SVG visualizers, lightweight games, and prompt-generated dashboards.\n- **Delivery**: The agent generates standalone HTML/CSS/JS (with embedded Tailwind CDN, React, Lucide, or ECharts).\n- **Execution in Frontend**: Render an isolated iframe with a strict security boundary:\n  ```tsx\n  <iframe\n    sandbox=\"allow-scripts allow-forms\"\n    srcDoc={sanitizedHtml}\n    title={item.name}\n    className=\"w-full h-[520px] rounded-[16px] border border-[var(--border)] bg-white shadow-inner\"\n  />\n  ```\n  *(Omitting `allow-same-origin` ensures the micro-app cannot access parent `window`, `localStorage`, auth tokens, or IndexedDB).*\n- **Responsive Viewport Controls**: Add responsive toggles (**Mobile 375px** | **Tablet 768px** | **Desktop 100%**) and a \"Pop Out into New Tab\" button.\n- **Home Dashboard Pinning (\"Add to Home Panels\")**: Users can click \"Pin to Home\" on any generated micro-app, persisting it into [`WidgetsRail.tsx`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/components/home/WidgetsRail.tsx) as a permanent interactive widget.\n\n#### Tier 2: Static Multi-File Web Projects (`web_bundle` Artifacts)\n- **Use Case**: React/Vite/Tailwind multi-file web apps built by the agent inside the Docker sandbox.\n- **Build & Archival**: The agent builds the project (`npm run build`), producing `/workspace/dist`. A new delivery tool archives the folder to the host's deliverable storage.\n- **Static Hosting Endpoint**: Add a static asset route in [`artifacts/router.py`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/backend/src/modules/artifacts/router.py):\n  `GET /api/v1/artifacts/{artifact_id}/site/{filepath:path}`\n  FastAPI serves the files directly from the host disk with sandboxed Content-Security-Policy headers:\n  `Content-Security-Policy: sandbox allow-scripts allow-forms; default-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' data: blob:; connect-src *`\n- **Zero Ongoing Container Overhead**: The built website remains permanently hosted on the backend host with zero background Docker containers running.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Third-Party Online Browser (Firecrawl / Browserbase)\n\nRather than running a resource-draining local Chromium farm, Vigil interfaces with cloud browser APIs using the user's API keys.\n\n### Tool Suite Specification (`backend/src/modules/runs/tools/browser.py`)\n\n```python\nclass BrowserNavigateArgs(BaseModel):\n    url: str = Field(..., description=\"Target web URL to navigate to\")\n    actions: list[dict[str, Any]] = Field(\n        default_factory=list,\n        description=\"Sequential actions: click, write, wait, press, scroll, screenshot\"\n    )\n\nclass BrowserExtractArgs(BaseModel):\n    url: str = Field(..., description=\"Target web page URL\")\n    prompt: str = Field(..., description=\"Extraction goal description\")\n    schema_definition: dict[str, Any] = Field(..., description=\"JSON Schema of required output\")\n```\n\n1. **`browser_navigate` (Powered by Firecrawl API)**:\n   - Dispatches to `POST https://api.firecrawl.dev/v1/scrape` using `FIRECRAWL_API_KEY`.\n   - Executes multi-step interaction scripts:\n     ```json\n     [\n       {\"type\": \"write\", \"text\": \"flight SFO to JFK\", \"selector\": \"input[name='q']\"},\n       {\"type\": \"press\", \"key\": \"Enter\"},\n       {\"type\": \"wait\", \"milliseconds\": 2000},\n       {\"type\": \"screenshot\"}\n     ]\n     ```\n   - Returns structured markdown plus a base64/URL screenshot of the resulting page.\n2. **`browser_extract`**:\n   - Uses Firecrawl’s LLM-based structured extraction to parse complex pages directly into validated JSON.\n3. **Live \"Handoff\" Window (Browserbase / Steel Integration)**:\n   - For complex, long-running web tasks, the tool provisions a session via Browserbase (`https://api.browserbase.com/v1/sessions`).\n   - Browserbase returns an interactive `session.liveUrl` debugging stream.\n   - Vigil's frontend embeds an inline iframe in the chat feed, enabling the user to watch the agent navigate, type, and click live, with the option to take over control.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Ultra-Fast Voice Input via Groq Whisper STT\n\n### Current Frontend Gap\nIn [`InputPill.tsx`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/components/chat/InputPill.tsx#L100-L104), audio capture is connected to an `AnalyserNode` for waveform animation, but stopping the microphone prints:\n`'Microphone stopped. Transcription is not connected yet.'`\n\n### Implementation Blueprint\n1. **Frontend Capture (`InputPill.tsx`)**:\n   - On `startCapture`, instantiate `MediaRecorder(stream, { mimeType: 'audio/webm;codecs=opus' })` (with fallback to `'audio/mp4'` for Safari).\n   - On `stopCapture`, assemble the recorded chunks into an audio Blob.\n   - Upload via `POST /api/v1/voice/transcribe` as multipart form data.\n   - Insert the transcribed text directly into `draft` state (`setDraft((prev) => (prev ? `${prev} ${text}` : text))`), allowing the user to review or edit before sending.\n2. **Backend Proxy (`backend/src/modules/voice/router.py`)**:\n   - Proxies the audio stream directly to Groq's Audio API (`https://api.groq.com/openai/v1/audio/transcriptions`) using `GROQ_API_KEY`:\n     ```python\n     @router.post(\"/transcribe\", response_model=VoiceTranscribeResponse)\n     async def transcribe_audio(\n         file: UploadFile = File(...),\n         settings: Settings = Depends(get_settings),\n     ) -> VoiceTranscribeResponse:\n         api_key = settings.GROQ_API_KEY\n         async with httpx.AsyncClient(timeout=30.0) as client:\n             res = await client.post(\n                 \"https://api.groq.com/openai/v1/audio/transcriptions\",\n                 headers={\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {api_key}\"},\n                 files={\"file\": (file.filename or \"audio.webm\", await file.read(), file.content_type)},\n                 data={\"model\": \"whisper-large-v3-turbo\", \"response_format\": \"json\"},\n             )\n             return VoiceTranscribeResponse(text=res.json()[\"text\"])\n     ```\n   - **Performance**: Latency for a 5-second voice memo is **120ms to 220ms**, providing near-instant transcription.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Decommissioning the Mascot & Adopting the Hark Aesthetic\n\n### 1. Removing `<EyeTracker />`\n- **Header**: In [`HeaderBrand.tsx`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/components/layout/HeaderBrand.tsx#L16-L20), remove `<EyeTracker />`. Replace with a refined typographic lockup: `Vigil` followed by a subtle geometric spark `✦` featuring an ambient breathing pulse.\n- **Landing Page**: In [`LandingRoute.tsx`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/routes/LandingRoute.tsx#L23), remove the eye-tracker. Replace the hero area with a live interactive showcase card demonstrating Hark-style proactivity cards and a micro-app preview.\n\n### 2. Hark Pro Visual Philosophy (Abidur Chowdhury Aesthetic)\n- **Palette**: Deep obsidian-to-midnight-navy (`#070A10` to `#0A0F1D`) in dark mode; tactile ivory/cream (`#FBF9F5` / `#FFFFFF`) in light mode.\n- **Squircle Ergonomics**: Organic continuous curvature (`rounded-[20px]` to `rounded-[28px]` on containers, `rounded-full` on pills and docks).\n- **Tactile Materiality**: Subdued borders (`rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08)`), micro-blur backdrops (`backdrop-blur-md`), and specular top-edge rim highlights.\n- **Zero AI Clutter**: Prohibit emoji icons in UI navigation; enforce clean, thin-stroke `lucide-react` vector glyphs (`strokeWidth={1.5}`).\n\n---\n\n## 6. Proactivity Tags & Verb-Based Action Triggers\n\n### The Interaction Model\nIn Hark Pro, tasks are framed around what the agent observed (proactivity tag) and what specific action it proposes to take (verb button):\n\n| Hark Pro Proactivity Tag | Context / Signal | Primary Verb Button | Secondary Action |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `✦ Michael wants to book an email` | Email inquiry received regarding Q4 figures | **`[ Draft ]`** | `[ Dismiss ]` |\n| `✦ Flight confirmed: SFO → JFK` | Flight booked, no hotel reservation found | **`[ Find Hotels ]`** | `[ Ignore ]` |\n| `✦ Stripe invoice due tomorrow ($120)` | SaaS subscription renewal notification | **`[ Pay ]`** | `[ Review Details ]` |\n| `✦ Overlapping calendar invitations` | Team sync conflicts with executive review | **`[ Reschedule ]`** | `[ Decline Sync ]` |\n| `✦ Figma team seats inactive (3 seats)` | Unused seats costing \\$45/mo | **`[ Cancel Seats ]`** | `[ Keep ]` |\n\n### Codebase Extensions\n1. **Schema Upgrade ([`cards/data.py`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/backend/src/modules/cards/data.py#L8-L16))**:\n   - Add `proactivity_tag: str | None = None` to `CardResponse`.\n   - Add `verb: str` to `CardActionSchema` (e.g. `\"draft\"`, `\"book\"`, `\"pay\"`, `\"rsvp\"`).\n2. **Dynamic Triage Synthesis ([`triage/service.py`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/backend/src/modules/triage/service.py#L127-L143))**:\n   - Replace the hardcoded `\"Quick Reply\"` and `\"Mark Done\"` defaults with LLM synthesis of contextual proactivity tags and active verbs.\n3. **Card Presentation ([`TaskCard.tsx`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/components/home/TaskCard.tsx#L95-L125))**:\n   - Render the `proactivity_tag` at the top of the card with an accented `✦` badge.\n   - Render the primary button as an active verb (e.g. `[ Draft ]`). Clicking it immediately triggers the workflow or deep-links into chat with pre-seeded intent.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Frictionless Human-in-the-Loop Inline Approvals\n\n### The Problem in Current Vigil\nIn [`ChatRoute.tsx`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/routes/ChatRoute.tsx#L94), the approval banner navigates to `/agent/approvals`. But **`/agent/approvals` does not exist in `App.tsx`**, causing it to fall through to `<Navigate to=\"/agent\" replace />`. In addition, not a single component in the frontend currently calls [`api.decideApproval()`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/queries/approvals.ts#L44).\n\n### The Inline Decision Card Solution\n- Remove the dead link to `/agent/approvals`.\n- When an execution step emits `event_type: \"approval_required\"`, render an **Inline Approval Card** directly inside the chat feed ([`ThinkingCapsule.tsx`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/components/chat/ThinkingCapsule.tsx#L996-L1002)):\n  - **Action Header**: e.g., `Send Email`, `Browser Purchase`, `Delete File`.\n  - **Parameter Diff**: Recipient address, message subject, order summary, or dollar amount.\n  - **Action Verbs**:\n    - Primary: **`[ Approve & Send ]`** or **`[ Authorize $45.00 ]`**.\n    - Secondary: **`[ Reject ]`** or **`[ Edit Parameters ]`**.\n- Clicking Approve invokes `api.decideApproval(approvalId, { decision: 'approved' })`. The backend marks the approval, enqueues `resume_run`, and execution resumes seamlessly without page reloads.\n\n---\n\n## 8. \"Secured by Hark\" Encrypted Vault & Dynamic MCP Connections\n\n### 1. Encrypted Credential Vault\n- Vigil already possesses robust AES-256-GCM encryption primitives in [`security.py`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/backend/src/config/security.py#L87-L120) and a `connected_accounts` database model.\n- **UI in Settings > Connectors**: Replace the empty placeholder in [`sections.tsx`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/components/settings/sections.tsx#L266-L326) with an interactive **Vault Management Center**:\n  - **API Keys**: Groq API Key (Voice STT), Firecrawl API Key (Web Browser), OpenAI/Anthropic Keys.\n  - **Service Integrations**: Google Workspace (Gmail/Calendar OAuth), GitHub, Slack.\n- Stored credentials are encrypted on write via `encrypt_secret(key, SECRET_KEY)` and decrypted strictly in memory when tools execute.\n\n### 2. Dynamic MCP (Model Context Protocol) Integration\n- **Fixing the Tool Schema Black Hole**: Currently, [`RunsService.build_loop()`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/backend/src/modules/runs/service.py#L522-L527) only checks `TOOLS` (Vigil's 12 built-in tools); discovered MCP tools are discarded and never passed to the LLM.\n- **Dynamic Schema Injection**:\n  1. Fetch active tools from `ConnectorsService.list_mcp_tools()`.\n  2. Convert each `MCPDiscoveredToolDTO` into standard OpenAI function declarations.\n  3. Merge them into `tool_schemas` passed to `build_loop()`.\n  4. Assign all external MCP tools to the `\"external\"` partition policy ([`state.py`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/backend/src/modules/runs/state.py#L270-L318)), ensuring that any third-party action automatically triggers an **inline approval card** before execution.\n\n---\n\n## 9. Comprehensive Comparison Matrix: Hark Pro vs. Adapted Vigil\n\n| Dimension | **Hark Pro** | **Current Vigil** | **Adapted Vigil (Open-Source Hark)** |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **Micro-Apps / Panels** | Cloud VM farm; creates dynamic full-screen widgets & panels | Monospace `<pre>` text in [`ArtifactCard.tsx`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/components/chat/ArtifactCard.tsx#L505); containers killed on exit | Sandboxed iframe preview (`allow-scripts allow-forms`), viewport toggles, static hosted asset bundles (`/artifacts/{id}/site/...`), home screen pinning |\n| **Web Browser** | Proprietary \"Handoff\" cloud browser computer | Exa semantic search/fetch only ([`search.py`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/backend/src/modules/runs/tools/search.py)); zero browser automation | Firecrawl API (actions: `click`, `write`, `screenshot`) with `FIRECRAWL_API_KEY`; Browserbase for live visual execution window |\n| **Voice STT** | Native voice mode / speech-to-text across iOS/Android/Web | Audio capture stub in [`InputPill.tsx`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/components/chat/InputPill.tsx#L103) (`Transcription is not connected yet`); no backend route | `MediaRecorder` + Groq Whisper API (`whisper-large-v3-turbo`) via `POST /api/v1/voice/transcribe` (<250ms latency) |\n| **Brand & Aesthetic** | Abidur Chowdhury Apple-inspired tactile design; no mascot | Cube eye-tracker mascot ([`EyeTracker.tsx`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/components/landing/EyeTracker.tsx)); ambient dark/light themes | Remove `<EyeTracker />`, minimalist `Vigil ✦` typography mark, warm tactile cream & obsidian palettes |\n| **Proactivity & Verbs** | Natural language observation tags; explicit verb buttons (`Draft`, `Book`, `Pay`) | Hardcoded \"Quick Reply\" / \"Mark Done\" in [`triage/service.py`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/backend/src/modules/triage/service.py#L128); generic `action_type` | Dynamic proactivity tags, explicit verb triggers (`[ Draft ]`, `[ RSVP ]`, `[ Pay ]`), open cards |\n| **Approvals Flow** | Frictionless inline decision checkpoints | `/agent/approvals` link is broken (404/redirect); `ThinkingCapsule` text-only; zero frontend calls to `decideApproval` | First-class inline approval cards in chat stream and home feed with verb confirmations and instant run resumption |\n| **Account Vault** | \"Secured by Hark\" encrypted vault for user logins, cards, and accounts | Schema exists (`connected_accounts`), AES-256-GCM in [`security.py`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/backend/src/config/security.py), but zero UI to add keys | Encrypted Credential Vault in Settings > Connectors; dynamic key resolution for tools |\n| **MCP Extensibility** | Native integration with web services | MCP integration layer exists in backend, but discovered tools are NEVER passed to LLM | Dynamic MCP tool schema injection into `RunLoop`; Settings UI for adding MCP servers; inline approval gating |\n\n---\n\n## 10. Suggested Phased Implementation Plan\n\n1. **Phase 1: Aesthetic & Interaction Core**\n   - Decommission `<EyeTracker />` from [`HeaderBrand.tsx`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/components/layout/HeaderBrand.tsx) and [`LandingRoute.tsx`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/routes/LandingRoute.tsx); introduce `Vigil ✦`.\n   - Extend `TaskCard.tsx` and triage schemas with proactivity tags and active verb buttons (`[ Draft ]`, `[ Book ]`).\n   - Fix approvals by deploying inline decision cards in chat and home feeds.\n2. **Phase 2: Micro-App Showcase & Voice Pipeline**\n   - Implement `srcDoc` sandboxed iframe previews in `ArtifactCard.tsx` with mobile/tablet/desktop viewport controls and home screen pinning.\n   - Implement `POST /api/v1/voice/transcribe` with Groq Whisper and wire `InputPill.tsx` audio capture.\n3. **Phase 3: Cloud Browser & Vault Extensibility**\n   - Add `browser_navigate` and `browser_extract` via Firecrawl in `tools/browser.py`.\n   - Build the Settings > Connectors & Vault UI for managing Groq, Firecrawl, and third-party API keys.\n   - Inject discovered MCP tool schemas dynamically into `RunsService.build_loop()`.","thinking":"The user wants to align the current project with an open-source architecture. The primary goal is adapting the existing design based on the open-source philosophy. Considering which parts to retain and which to adjust based on the open-source design is the next step.\n\n\nThe open-source design emphasizes mirroring core functionalities. The sandbox environment should mimic the VM farm, incorporating browser capabilities. Leveraging a third-party online browser like Firecrawl will provide the necessary API key support, avoiding the need for a dedicated virtual machine. Speech-to-text functionality will be integrated via an STT model, possibly using GROQ API. The mascot element is less critical compared to accurately mirroring the core aesthetic, design language, and interactive elements such as proactive tags and verb-based buttons. Deeper research is necessary to fully align the design.\n\n\nReviewing the subagent's work confirms alignment with the open-source philosophy by mirroring core functionalities. The proposed sandbox architecture addresses website display and browser requirements using iframes and static web apps. STT integration is specified with GROQ API, and the mascot removal aligns with the minimalist design principles. Further checks on account support and MCP connections are required to fully verify the requirements.\n\n\n"}
