b) Capability showcase (polished visual and interactive experience)\n- (c) Exploration / prototype\n- (d) OPEN (let the team decide)\n*Default: (a) Production*\n\n2. **Scope & Phasing**\nThe implementation plan details four parts: Part I (Design System tokens & motion), Part II (UI components & mascot removal), Part III (Pluggable MCP factory & tool registry), and Part IV (Firecrawl browser, Groq Whisper STT, Vault backend). Which scope should be tackled in this run?\n- (a) All four parts (complete implementation plan)\n- (b) Focus first on Part I & Part II (design system & UI components)\n- (c) OPEN (let the team decide)\n*Default: (a) All four parts*\n\n3. **Approach & Restrictions**\nWhich of these should the team NOT be allowed to do? (choose (e) if there are no restrictions)\n- (a) Copy code from existing open-source projects for core logic\n- (b) Use pre-built libraries or frameworks for core functionality\n- (c) Run external scripts or delegate execution to other tools\n- (d) Read test source code to understand expected behaviour before implementing\n- (e) None of these: no restrictions, any approach that works\n*Default: (e) None of these (if Question 1 is chosen as Capability showcase, forbidding (a) and (c) is suggested)*\n\n4. **External Integrations & API Keys**\nParts III & IV introduce integrations with external services (Firecrawl API, Groq Whisper API, dynamic MCP transports). How should these be handled when live external API keys are not present in the environment?\n- (a) Provide fallback/mock modes so all features and automated tests pass without requiring external API keys\n- (b) Require active API keys and live external endpoints\n- (c) OPEN (let the team decide)\n*Default: (a) Provide fallback/mock modes so all features and automated tests pass without requiring external API keys*\n\n5. **Verification Resources**\nWhich test suites or verification commands should the team run to verify the changes?\n- (a) Existing repository checks (e.g. frontend typecheck/lint/build in `web/` and backend pytest in `backend/`)\n- (b) Custom verification script or commands (please specify)\n- (c) OPEN (let the team decide)\n*Default: (a) Existing repository checks*\n</SYSTEM_MESSAGE>"}
