re.\n4. Any change, however small, comes back to my conversation id (`e23352ee-50b5-436b-9dd2-a087c7382607`), and forward only the latest draft's marked text or feedback.\n5. If you have nobody to ask, answer and approve for yourself from the request and your own context.\n\nExpecting this to run as a full four-part project across the frontend design system, UI components, backend MCP factory, and external integrations; say so if you want it phased or scoped differently.\n\nBEGIN PROMPT\nuse subagents to write the code. They should use the 3.8 flash high model. Your usage limits (ARGON) is low so weaker models need to write the code. Transform Vigil into an open-source counterpart to Hark Pro across the design system, UI components, pluggable MCP factory, and external integrations for production use.\n\nWorking directory: /home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent\nIntegrity mode: development\n\n## Requirements\n\n### R1. Hark Pro Design System & Visual Tokens\nImplement the dual-theme design system in `web/src/styles/tokens.css` with Obsidian Horizon (`[data-theme='dark']`) and Tactile Alabaster (`[data-theme='light']`) palettes. Define visual tokens for proactivity tags, verb pills, approval surfaces, specular rim highlights (`inset 0 1px 0 0 ...`), Plus Jakarta Sans typography scale (`--font-sans`), squircle geometry radii (`24px`, `20px`, `18px`, `26px`, `rounded-full`), and the 17-point CSS `linear()` spring curve (`--ease-spring`).\n\n### R2. UI Component Architecture & Mascot Decommissioning\nDecommission the `<EyeTracker />` companion mascot from `web/src/components/layout/HeaderBrand.tsx`, `web/src/routes/LandingRoute.tsx`, and `web/src/styles/tokens.css`, replacing it with the minimalist `Vigil ✦` vector spark brand mark. Extend backend schemas (`backend/src/modules/cards/data.py`, `backend/src/schemas/triage.py`) and triage service (`backend/src/modules/triage/service.py`) to generate proactivity tags and active verbs. Update `NotificationCard.tsx` and