{"step_index":84,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-10T18:50:54Z","input_tokens":2618,"cache_read_tokens":143332,"output_tokens":975,"content":"All Hark Pro research findings, comparative analyses, UI/UX design guidelines, and technical architecture specifications have been compiled into a permanent specification file in the repository:\n\n📄 **[`docs/HARK_PRO_SPECIFICATION.md`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/docs/HARK_PRO_SPECIFICATION.md)**  \n*(with a quick-reference link at the repository root in [`HARK_PRO.md`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/HARK_PRO.md))*\n\n### What is Documented in the Specification:\n\n1. **Platform Provenance & Philosophy**:\n   - Background on Brett Adcock (Figure AI, Archer Aviation), lead designer Abidur Chowdhury (ex-Apple iPhone Air), and the *\"Macintosh GUI for AI\"* philosophy rejecting raw conversational chat terminals in favor of an ambient OS and living canvas.\n\n2. **Full Comparative Analysis (Hark Pro vs. Vigil)**:\n   - Detailed matrix comparing task execution, visual observability, proactivity models, information architecture, voice, browsers, mascots, and motion engines.\n\n3. **Complete UI/UX Design System Guidelines**:\n   - **Color Palettes**: Exact tokens for **Obsidian Horizon (Dark)** (`#06070A` $\\rightarrow$ `#0C0F17`) and **Tactile Alabaster (Light)** (`#FAF8F5` $\\rightarrow$ `#F0ECE1`), warm dawn amber accents (`#E88449` / `#C86428`), and Apple-style specular top-rim catchlights (`inset 0 1px 0 0 ...`).\n   - **Typography & Scale**: Geometric font feature settings for `Plus Jakarta Sans Variable` across display greetings, section headers, card titles, editorial body text, verb buttons, proactivity pills, and tabular code.\n   - **Squircle Geometry**: Concentric radii (`24px` panels, `20px` cards, `18px` checkpoints, `26px` composers, `9999px` rounded-full buttons) and 3px urgency rails.\n   - **Motion Physics**: The 17-point CSS `linear()` spring curve with 2.8% overshoot (`--ease-spring`).\n\n4. **Interaction Patterns & Component Anatomy**:\n   - **Mascot Decommissioning**: Replacing `<EyeTracker />` with the minimalist `Vigil ✦` vector spark.\n   - **Proactivity Tags & Verb Buttons**: Natural language observations (`✦ Michael wants to schedule a review`) with active verbs (`[ Draft ]`, `[ Book ]`, `[ Pay ]`, `[ RSVP ]`, `[ Cancel ]`).\n   - **Inline Approvals**: Resolving the broken approvals route with first-class `InlineApprovalCard` components directly inside the conversation stream.\n   - **Micro-App Showcase**: Dual-tier sandboxed execution (`srcDoc` iframes with mobile/tablet/desktop switchers and dashboard pinning, plus static site bundle hosting via CSP).\n   - **Sub-250ms Voice STT**: Groq Whisper (`whisper-large-v3-turbo`) integration with client-side `MediaRecorder` WebM/Opus streaming.\n\n5. **Backend & Architecture**:\n   - **Third-Party Cloud Browser**: Firecrawl API scraping, sequential actions, and structured schema extraction.\n   - **Pluggable MCP Factory Pattern**: Uniform `MCPTransportProtocol`, stdio (with vault secret env injection), SSE, 1-click presets (`firecrawl`, `github`, `filesystem`, `postgres`, `linear`), and dynamic LLM tool bridging with approval partitioning.\n   - **Encrypted Credential Vault**: AES-256-GCM encrypted secrets in Settings > Connectors.\n\n6. **Codebase Discrepancies & Corrections**:\n   - Documented fixes for routing hierarchy, container teardown lifecycle, approvals navigation, triage hardcoding, and MCP tool schema exposure."}
