{"step_index":262,"source":"SYSTEM","type":"CHECKPOINT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-11T10:06:35Z","input_tokens":3872,"cache_read_tokens":253826,"output_tokens":2619,"content":"# Resuming from a compaction\n\nYou are continuing work on the task described above, but you have lost access to the full conversation history, and need to resume work efficiently using the progress summary below:\n\n# User Requests\nThe following were user requests from the truncated conversation in chronological order:\n1. /boost Invetigate the HARK pro platform from a UI UX persepective and compare it to vigil. The way it responds to tasks, its proactivity, the way it showcases information, the way it communicate, the interactivity of the cat and so on. Please be exhasutive in your research\n2. /boost The issue now is that this project is designed to be an open-source HARK Pro, and that is just it. The nature of it is that potentially we could try to modify our architecture to meet theirs, so we can just try to adapt it. So the good on our end, we can try to keep. The bad, we can try to adjust, but I think I like their design philosophy a lot, so I want it to mirror that design philosophy. So for now, we'll just try to let it run in a sandbox, but the primary features that their AI model has includes things like the ability to actually build small websites and showcase it to the users, which our sandbox does not have. So our sandbox should actually mirror their VM farm, if you get where I'm coming from. So it should be able to mirror the core functionalities, including the browser. So for the browser, we'll make use of a third-party online browser, something like the Firecrawl browser or something like that, so we'll have proper support for the API keys as opposed to running a dedicated virtual machine. Voice, we will make use of an STT model, probably something using the GROQ API for the voice, that being the speech-to-text. The companion mascot can be removed for now. It isn't something that is very required, this is the core necessity, but their general design language and aesthetic is something that should be mirrored, as it is one of the core functionalities of their platform, something that people genuinely like. So the way they go about approvals, the way they go about even the widgets, the way they go about things like the proactivity tags. For example, you can see a tag like Michael wants to book an email, then you see a button there that says Draft, indicating that it's going to draft the email. So the buttons there are actually verbs, if you get where I'm coming from. So the whole design, I need you to conduct deeper research and update your findings in order to suit the new requirements of the project. Also consider things like the account support, the MCP connections, and so on. \n3. TURN THIS TO A STRONG IMPLEMENTATION PLAN. BRING SPECIFICS LIKE COLOR COMPOSITION, SIZING, COLOR AND SO ON FOR THE USE. ALSO THE BEST WAY TO GO ABOUT REGISTERING mcPS EASILY POTENTIALLY USING A FACTORY PATTERN AND SO ON. (THE UI IS EXTREMLY IMPORTANT)\n4. /teamwork use subagents to write the code. They should use the 3.8 flash high model. Your usage limits (ARGON) is low so weaker models need to write the code\n5. i approve\n6. Please turn all the hark pro findingd, design guidlines and so on into a fie in the repo\n7. As far as the UI goes, you didn't get the UI, so I'm giving you these screenshots to try to explain how the UI is supposed to look like as far as the HARK Pro platform is to go. That is just one thing that I want to shed light on. The general structure is a bit off as far as the UI design is to go. I gave you samples of the dark theme and light theme. The dark theme samples are not that many that I provided you, but that is how the background is meant to look like. Potentially, you need to separately examine the background for the light theme and the dark theme to properly just get a feel of it. The nature of the platform is such that as of right now, you can completely discard the way the navbar is being designed, the home page, and everything, keeping everything in one unified page with toggles to move between them relatively quickly. There is a centralized view of the platform where you do not show the widgets. The widgets view has been provided as well, where you see the time in place of the widget section. I think that is useful for the design as well. In conjecture, there are sample pictures provided for the other pages, the general look and feel. I feel like this should be a guide that you should use. Maybe you can use this to dispatch another designer to modify the generalized design, or you can use it to steer the current UI components implementation. \n  - [Attachment: image/png (/home/nasbombz/.gemini/antigravity/brain/4c9225c7-9a87-4aee-bca4-891ac270da2a/.user_uploaded/media_1794336791572_accff37b.jpg)]\n  - [Attachment: image/png (/home/nasbombz/.gemini/antigravity/brain/4c9225c7-9a87-4aee-bca4-891ac270da2a/.user_uploaded/media_1794336809063_d470144a.jpg)]\n  - [Attachment: image/png (/home/nasbombz/.gemini/antigravity/brain/4c9225c7-9a87-4aee-bca4-891ac270da2a/.user_uploaded/media_1794336824522_aacb669d.jpg)]\n  - [Attachment: image/png (/home/nasbombz/.gemini/antigravity/brain/4c9225c7-9a87-4aee-bca4-891ac270da2a/.user_uploaded/media_1794336846627_6550ceb2.jpg)]\n  - [Attachment: image/png (/home/nasbombz/.gemini/antigravity/brain/4c9225c7-9a87-4aee-bca4-891ac270da2a/.user_uploaded/media_1794336863617_4cdbb3cc.jpg)]\n  - [Attachment: image/png (/home/nasbombz/.gemini/antigravity/brain/4c9225c7-9a87-4aee-bca4-891ac270da2a/.user_uploaded/media_1794336878629_d2da638e.jpg)]\n  - [Attachment: image/png (/home/nasbombz/.gemini/antigravity/brain/4c9225c7-9a87-4aee-bca4-891ac270da2a/.user_uploaded/media_1794336895259_12128f2c.jpg)]\n  - [Attachment: image/png (/home/nasbombz/.gemini/antigravity/brain/4c9225c7-9a87-4aee-bca4-891ac270da2a/.user_uploaded/media_1794336932722_469fb2f7.jpg)]\n  - [Attachment: image/png (/home/nasbombz/.gemini/antigravity/brain/4c9225c7-9a87-4aee-bca4-891ac270da2a/.user_uploaded/media_1794336946036_b6bb06a4.jpg)]\n  - [Attachment: image/png (/home/nasbombz/.gemini/antigravity/brain/4c9225c7-9a87-4aee-bca4-891ac270da2a/.user_uploaded/media_1794337031632_c639a127.jpg)]\n8. continue\n9. continue\n10. It seems like the chnage cant reflect in the UI\n\n<summary>\n## 1. Task Overview\n- **Core Request**: Research and transform the Vigil platform (`/home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent`) to mirror **Hark Pro** from a UI/UX, product philosophy, and technical architecture perspective. Based on 10 user-provided production screenshots of Hark Pro (both dark and light themes), evolve Vigil from its legacy multi-page layout into Hark Pro's unified single-page living canvas.\n- **Key Capabilities Required**:\n  1. **Living Atmospheric Cloud Backdrop**: Warm sand/ivory peach cloudscape in light mode (`#FAF4EE`, `#E8DDD0`, `#DFD0C0`), moody dusky charcoal/plum/slate in dark mode (`#121016`, `#18151f`, smoky plum drifts), with fine photographic grain and specular rim catchlights (`inset 0 1px 0 ...`).\n  2. **Top Floating Chrome**: Home squircle button `[ ⌂ ]` (`44x44px`, `rounded-[14px]`), floating segmented switch `[ Chat | Projects ]` (`rounded-full`, `h-8`), and right-aligned pill `[ Search ]` + circular User Avatar (`N`).\n  3. **Adaptive 4-State Left Column**:\n     - *Widgets/Panels*: Weather card (`Ojota, NG`, 27°C, sunset), Usage limit card, Calendar card, `+ Create a new panel`.\n     - *Typographic Clock*: Large live editorial date/clock (`Tue \\n Nov 10 \\n 6:56 PM`).\n     - *Projects Index*: `New project`, `FYP`, sub-folders (`• PROJECT IDEAS`, `• Software Developer Interview Prep`, `Awun`).\n     - *Collapsed/Centralized*: Left column collapses completely, centering the central chat feed.\n  4. **Proactivity Tags & Embedded Verb Buttons**: Exact Hark Pro format `[ [Accept] Boardy's 5:30 PM Maji invite... ⌝ ]` and `[ [Draft] a note asking Boardy... ⌝ ]`.\n  5. **Live Browser Execution Window**: Embedded rounded squircle browser preview in the feed with floating status pill (`● Error` in `#DC2626` / `● Active` in `#10B981`) and expand button `⛶`.\n  6. **Inline Approvals & Structured Cards**: Replace broken `/agent/approvals` route with inline `InlineApprovalCard.tsx` and structured email draft cards (`Reply to Boardy and Shubham`).\n  7. **Micro-App Sandboxing**: `ArtifactCard.tsx` with `sandbox=\"allow-scripts allow-forms\"`, viewport switchers (375px/768px/100%), and home dashboard pinning.\n  8. **Pluggable MCP Factory Pattern**: `backend/src/integrations/mcp/factory.py` with stdio (vault env secret injection), SSE (vault header injection), 1-click presets (`firecrawl`, `github`, `filesystem`, `postgres`, `linear`), and `MCPToolAdapterFactory` dynamic tool bridging into `build_loop()`.\n  9. **Cloud Browser (Firecrawl) & Voice STT (Groq Whisper)**: `browser_navigate`/`browser_extract` with screenshot artifacts; `POST /api/v1/voice/transcribe` with Groq `whisper-large-v3-turbo` connected to `InputPill.tsx` `MediaRecorder`.\n  10. **Encrypted Vault (\"Secured by Vigil\")**: AES-256-GCM vault in Settings > Connectors.\n  11. **Mascot Decommissioning**: Retire `<EyeTracker />` toy; replace with `Vigil ✦` vector spark.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Progress\n- **Specification Documentation**:\n  - `docs/HARK_PRO_SPECIFICATION.md`: Comprehensive 500+ line living design system and architectural specification.\n  - `HARK_PRO.md`: Top-level repo guide pointing to the specification.\n  - `implementation_plan.md`: Artifact generated for review.\n- **Backend Implementation & Test Validation**:\n  - `backend/src/integrations/mcp/factory.py`: Pluggable MCP factory with stdio/SSE transports, presets, and vault injection.\n  - `backend/src/modules/runs/tools/mcp_bridge.py`: Dynamic adapter bridging MCP tool schemas into Vigil `Tool` instances.\n  - `backend/src/modules/runs/tools/browser.py`: Firecrawl browser navigation, DOM actions, and schema extraction with screenshot artifacts.\n  - `backend/src/modules/voice/router.py`: Groq Whisper audio transcription route registered in `backend/src/config/router.py`.\n  - `backend/src/modules/settings/vault.py`: Encrypted secret vault handling.\n  - `backend/alembic/versions/0009_card_proactivity_and_verbs.py`: Database migration for `proactivity_tag` and active `verb`.\n  - Backend test suites executed: **820 passed, 11 skipped, 1 xfailed** in 400.17s across all unit and integration tests.\n- **Frontend Architecture & Components Built**:\n  - `web/src/components/layout/AmbientBackground.tsx`: Updated with warm peach/sand cloudscape (light mode) and moody charcoal/plum cloudscape (dark mode).\n  - `web/src/components/hark/HarkTopChrome.tsx`: Home button `[ ⌂ ]`, segmented pill switch `[ Chat | Projects ]`, `[ Search ]` pill, and user avatar.\n  - `web/src/components/hark/HarkLeftRail.tsx`: Implements all 4 states (`widgets`, `clock`, `projects`, `collapsed`).\n  - `web/src/components/hark/HarkSearchModal.tsx`: Floating centered search pill with backdrop blur.\n  - `web/src/components/hark/HarkProfileSheet.tsx`: iOS/macOS-style grouped settings sheet.\n  - `web/src/components/hark/HarkProactivityPill.tsx`: Exact Hark Pro pill format `[ [Verb]  Observation... ⌝ ]`.\n  - `web/src/components/hark/HarkLiveBrowserCard.tsx`: Embedded live browser card with status badge and expand toggle.\n  - `web/src/components/hark/HarkEmailCard.tsx`: Structured email draft card with prompt questions.\n  - `web/src/components/hark/HarkUnifiedApp.tsx`: Central coordinator binding the top chrome, adaptive left rail, feed, and bottom composer.\n  - `web/src/routes/HomeRoute.tsx` & `web/src/routes/ChatRoute.tsx`: Both updated to render `HarkUnifiedApp`.\n  - `web/src/App.tsx`: Removed `FloatingDock` and `HeaderBrand` from `AppShell`.\n  - `web/src/styles/tokens.css`: Updated with Hark Pro cloud tokens, palettes, and linear spring physics.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Key Findings\n- **Why the UI Changes Didn't Reflect Initially**:\n  - Vigil was historically architected as a standard multi-page web app with fixed `HeaderBrand` at the top and `FloatingDock` (bottom glass bar with Home/Chat/Settings icons) wrapping an `<Outlet />` that swapped between `HomeView` (which had a hardcoded cards + right sidebar grid) and `ChatRoute` (a separate full-screen chat).\n  - Component edits made to individual subcomponents inside `TaskCard` or `NotificationCard` did not change the global shell layout.\n  - To match Hark Pro, the entire multi-page shell needed to be replaced with `HarkUnifiedApp`, putting the living canvas, top floating chrome, 4-state left rail, and unified chat/projects feed directly into `App.tsx` and the primary routes.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Errors & Fixes\n- **Error 1: TypeScript Unused Variable and Props Mismatches on Build**:\n  - *Details*: `HarkEmailCard.tsx` had unused `Send`/`onSend`; `HarkLeftRail.tsx` had unused `CloudSun`/`TrendingUp`; `HarkLiveBrowserCard.tsx` had unused `fullscreen`; `HarkUnifiedApp.tsx` was missing required `emptyHint` prop on `MessageStream` and had a 2-arg `onSend` callback mismatch with `InputPill`.\n  - *Fix*: Cleaned up unused imports/variables, wired `fullscreen` to toggle card width/height, added `emptyHint={<div />}`, and adapted `InputPill` `onSend={(text) => chat.send(text)}`.\n- **Error 2: Teamwork Subagent Quota Cooldown (429)**:\n  - *Details*: Teamwork orchestrator hit an API quota pause during M4 audit.\n  - *Fix*: Handled gracefully with clean handover and verified state preservation once cooldown cleared.\n- **Error 3: Card Persistence Gap in Triage Pipeline**:\n  - *Details*: Adversarial test caught that `proactivity_tag` was not persisted across all database write paths.\n  - *Fix*: Created Alembic migration `0009_card_proactivity_and_verbs.py` and updated `CardsService` repository write methods.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Active Context\n- **Workspace**: `/home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent`\n- **Subagents**: Previous subagents terminated cleanly after milestone completion and server restart.\n- **Environment**: Linux, Python 3.12 (via `uv`), Node.js (via `pnpm`). Both frontend and backend are buildable and passing tests.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Next Steps (Immediate Resumption Checklist)\n1. **Run Frontend Typecheck & Build**:\n   ```bash\n   cd /home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web && pnpm typecheck && pnpm build\n   ```\n   Verify 0 errors.\n2. **Start Dev Server & Verify Visual Output**:\n   Run the local startup script:\n   ```bash\n   ./start.sh --mock\n   ```\n   or start Vite directly:\n   ```bash\n   cd web && pnpm dev\n   ```\n   Open `http://localhost:5173/agent` and verify:\n   - Floating top chrome: Home squircle button `[ ⌂ ]`, `[ Chat | Projects ]` pill switch, `[ Search ]`, and circular avatar.\n   - Clicking `[ ⌂ ]` cycles through: Widgets panel $\\rightarrow$ Typographic clock $\\rightarrow$ Collapsed/centralized mode.\n   - Atmospheric cloud backdrop reflects the warm sand/peach (light mode) or dusky charcoal/plum (dark mode).\n   - Proactivity tags with embedded verb buttons `[ [Accept] ... ⌝ ]` and `[ [Draft] ... ⌝ ]` render in the feed.\n   - Embedded browser execution window and email draft card render cleanly.\n   - Clicking `Search` opens the centered search pill modal.\n   - Clicking the user avatar opens the Hark Pro settings sheet.\n3. **Commit & Push / Finalize Repository State**:\n   Commit the unified Hark Pro components, tokens, specifications, and test suites with a clean descriptive commit message.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Commitments & Constraints\n- Keep all code strictly conforming to the Hark Pro production screenshots provided by the user.\n- Strictly maintain 0 lint/TypeScript errors and 100% backend test pass rates.\n- Do not re-introduce the cartoon mascot (`EyeTracker`) or the legacy `FloatingDock` bottom bar.\n</summary>\n\nYou have the 13 following artifacts written to the artifacts directory:\n