{"step_index":353,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-11T10:13:23Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-11T10:13:23Z\nCompleted At: 2026-11-11T10:13:23Z\nShowing lines 375-410 of 434\n375: \n376: \n377: def resolve_verdicts(\n378:     units: Sequence[HistoryUnit],\n379:     tier1: Tier1Result,\n380:     tier0: Tier0Selection,\n381: ) -> dict[str, Verdict]:\n382:     \"\"\"Apply the Tier 0 lock to every Tier 1 verdict.\n383: \n384:     This function is the single place where the safety lock is enforced. A\n385:     locked unit keeps the verdict RETAIN whatever Tier 1 says.\n386:     \"\"\"\n387:     resolved: dict[str, Verdict] = {}\n388:     for unit in units:\n389:         if tier0.is_locked(unit.unit_id):\n390:             resolved[unit.unit_id] = Verdict.RETAIN\n391:             continue\n392:         score = tier1.score_for(unit.unit_id)\n393:         resolved[unit.unit_id] = Verdict.RETAIN if score is None else score.verdict\n394:     return resolved\n395: \n396: \n397: # =============================================================================\n398: # Provider tokenizer\n399: # =============================================================================\n400: \n401: @lru_cache(maxsize=16)\n402: def _encoding(model: str):\n403:     \"\"\"Return the provider tokenizer encoding for a model name.\"\"\"\n404:     if tiktoken is None:\n405:         raise TokenizerError(\"tiktoken is not installed. Token counting cannot use an estimate.\")\n406:     try:\n407:         return tiktoken.encoding_for_model(model)\n408:     except KeyError:\n409:         return tiktoken.get_encoding(DEFAULT_ENCODING_NAME)\n410: "}
{"step_index":354,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-11T10:13:23Z","input_tokens":2106,"cache_read_tokens":100972,"output_tokens":1005,"thinking":"The absence of a `jev_client` leads to all units being assigned a \"RETAIN\" verdict. This happens because the scoring function returns `None` when the client is missing. Consequently, no messages are stubbed or dropped. The summarizer is never invoked, and zero tokens are saved due to the consistent \"RETAIN\" verdict.\n\n\nThe current setup ensures no compaction, leading to excessive token usage due to an always-growing context window. The token limit is set so high that compaction never activates, resulting in continuous accumulation of messages. Specifically, when the `jev_client` is unavailable, or a unit is older than the recent window, the historical user messages must be eligible for summarization into the summary block. Intelligent heuristic classification needs to be in place as a fallback for the old tool results with larger outputs or artifacts, marking them as `STUB`.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"grep -rn \"build_tools\" backend/src/","WaitMsBeforeAsync":5000,"toolSummary":"Find build_tools"}}]}
