{"step_index":367,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-11T10:14:15Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-11T10:14:15Z\nCompleted At: 2026-11-11T10:14:15Z\nShowing lines 543-630 of 941\n543: class RunToolExecutor:\n544:     \"\"\"Run the tools of one run.\n545: \n546:     A local tool runs inside one sandbox container per run. The container is\n547:     created on the first local call and removed by ``close``. An external tool\n548:     runs through the connector host, because the user approved it.\n549: \n550:     The class satisfies :class:`src.modules.runs.loop.ToolExecutor`.\n551:     \"\"\"\n552: \n553:     #: Tools that need no run container. They run on the host, or, for\n554:     #: ``ask_user``, only return a pending marker. ``execute`` gives them the\n555:     #: ``host-only`` container id so no sandbox is created for them.\n556:     HOST_ONLY_TOOLS: frozenset[str] = frozenset(\n557:         {\n558:             \"web_search\",\n559:             \"web_fetch\",\n560:             \"manage_tasks\",\n561:             \"ask_user\",\n562:             \"browser_navigate\",\n563:             \"browser_extract\",\n564:         }\n565:     )\n566: \n567: \n568:     def __init__(\n569:         self,\n570:         *,\n571:         session: AsyncSession | None,\n572:         settings: Settings,\n573:         run_id: UUID,\n574:         sandbox: SandboxRunnerProtocol,\n575:         mcp_host: MCPHostProtocol,\n576:         delivery_dir: Any | None = None,\n577:         connector_id: str = \"default\",\n578:     ) -> None:\n579:         self.session = session\n580:         self.settings = settings\n581:         self.run_id = run_id\n582:         self.sandbox = sandbox\n583:         self.mcp_host = mcp_host\n584:         self.connector_id = connector_id\n585:         base_path = Path(settings.WORKSPACE_BASE_PATH)\n586:         if delivery_dir is None:\n587:             try:\n588:                 base_path.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n589:             except OSError:\n590:                 base_path = Path(\"/tmp/vigil/workspaces\")\n591:                 base_path.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n592:         self.delivery_dir = (\n593:             delivery_dir\n594:             if delivery_dir is not None\n595:             else base_path / \"delivery\" / str(run_id)\n596:         )\n597:         self.snapshot_tar = (\n598:             base_path / \"snapshots\" / f\"{run_id}.tar\"\n599:         )\n600:         self._container_id: str | None = None\n601: \n602:     @property\n603:     def container_id(self) -> str | None:\n604:         \"\"\"Return the container id of this run, or None before the first call.\"\"\"\n605:         return self._container_id\n606: \n607:     async def start(self) -> str:\n608:         \"\"\"Create the run container once and return its id.\"\"\"\n609:         if self._container_id is None:\n610:             self._container_id = await self._create_container()\n611:             restore: Any = getattr(self.sandbox, \"restore_workspace\", None)\n612:             if callable(restore) and self.snapshot_tar.is_file():\n613:                 try:\n614:                     await restore(self._container_id, str(self.snapshot_tar))\n615:                 except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001\n616:                     pass\n617:         return self._container_id\n618: \n619:     async def close(self) -> None:\n620:         \"\"\"Snapshot the workspace and tear down the run container.\"\"\"\n621:         if self._container_id is not None:\n622:             container_id = self._container_id\n623:             self._container_id = None\n624:             snapshot: Any = getattr(self.sandbox, \"snapshot_workspace\", None)\n625:             if callable(snapshot):\n626:                 try:\n627:                     self.snapshot_tar.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n628:                     await snapshot(container_id, str(self.snapshot_tar))\n629:                 except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001\n630:                     pass"}
