{"step_index":371,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-11T10:14:24Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-11T10:14:24Z\nCompleted At: 2026-11-11T10:14:25Z\nShowing lines 1-100 of 272\n1: \"\"\"Core tool harness: nine stateless tools over the sandbox runner.\n2: \n3: Every tool declares a name, a JSON schema, and an approval level. The level is ``read``,\n4: ``local`` or ``external``. A call validates its arguments against the tool schema first.\n5: Only then does the handler run. The handler calls the sandbox runner protocol or it\n6: writes a file to the delivery directory.\n7: \n8: A call returns a :class:`ToolResult` with ``{ok, content, artifact_ref, error}``. A tool\n9: never raises across this boundary. Approval logic is not here. V-07 owns the approval\n10: gate. ``ask_user`` is the only ``external`` tool. It returns a pending marker and does\n11: not block.\n12: \"\"\"\n13: from __future__ import annotations\n14: \n15: import inspect\n16: from collections.abc import Awaitable, Callable, Mapping, Sequence\n17: from dataclasses import dataclass\n18: from pathlib import Path\n19: from types import MappingProxyType\n20: from typing import Any, Literal\n21: \n22: from pydantic import BaseModel, ConfigDict, Field, ValidationError\n23: \n24: from src.integrations.repositories import SandboxRunnerProtocol\n25: \n26: ApprovalLevel = Literal[\"read\", \"local\", \"external\"]\n27: \n28: #: Every approval level that a tool can declare.\n29: APPROVAL_LEVELS: tuple[ApprovalLevel, ...] = (\"read\", \"local\", \"external\")\n30: \n31: #: The harness exposes built-in tools.\n32: TOOL_COUNT = 14\n33: \n34: \n35: class ToolResult(BaseModel):\n36:     \"\"\"The structured result of one tool call.\n37: \n38:     The object has the four keys of the tool call contract. ``content`` holds the tool\n39:     output. ``artifact_ref`` holds a host path when the tool produced a file. ``error``\n40:     holds a message when ``ok`` is false.\n41:     \"\"\"\n42: \n43:     model_config = ConfigDict(frozen=True)\n44: \n45:     ok: bool = Field(..., description=\"True when the call succeeded.\")\n46:     content: Any = Field(\n47:         default=None,\n48:         description=\"Tool output. A string, a dictionary, or null.\",\n49:     )\n50:     artifact_ref: str | None = Field(\n51:         default=None,\n52:         description=\"Host path of a produced file, or null.\",\n53:     )\n54:     error: str | None = Field(\n55:         default=None,\n56:         description=\"Failure message when ok is false, else null.\",\n57:     )\n58: \n59:     @classmethod\n60:     def success(cls, content: Any = None, *, artifact_ref: str | None = None) -> \"ToolResult\":\n61:         \"\"\"Build a successful result.\"\"\"\n62:         return cls(ok=True, content=content, artifact_ref=artifact_ref, error=None)\n63: \n64:     @classmethod\n65:     def failure(cls, error: str, *, content: Any = None) -> \"ToolResult\":\n66:         \"\"\"Build a failed result.\"\"\"\n67:         return cls(ok=False, content=content, artifact_ref=None, error=error)\n68: \n69: \n70: @dataclass(frozen=True)\n71: class ToolContext:\n72:     \"\"\"The runner and the delivery directory for one tool call.\n73: \n74:     The context holds no state. The caller builds it for each call.\n75:     \"\"\"\n76: \n77:     runner: SandboxRunnerProtocol\n78:     container_id: str\n79:     delivery_dir: Path\n80: \n81: \n82: Handler = Callable[[Any, ToolContext], Awaitable[ToolResult]]\n83: \n84: \n85: @dataclass(frozen=True)\n86: class Tool:\n87:     \"\"\"One tool: a name, a description, a JSON schema, a level, and a handler.\"\"\"\n88: \n89:     name: str\n90:     description: str\n91:     level: ApprovalLevel\n92:     args_model: type[BaseModel]\n93:     handler: Handler\n94:     input_schema: dict[str, Any]\n95: \n96:     @classmethod\n97:     def define(\n98:         cls,\n99:         *,\n100:         name: str,"}
