{"step_index":408,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-11T10:17:20Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-11T10:17:20Z\nCompleted At: 2026-11-11T10:17:21Z\nShowing lines 110-180 of 203\n110:     if (IS_MOCK) {\n111:       set({ status: 'authed', device: MOCK_DEVICE });\n112:       return;\n113:     }\n114: \n115:     const stored = await readStoredSession();\n116:     if (!stored) {\n117:       setBearerToken(null);\n118:       set({ status: 'unauthed', device: null });\n119:       return;\n120:     }\n121: \n122:     setBearerToken(stored.token);\n123:     try {\n124:       const device = await me();\n125:       set({ status: 'authed', device });\n126:     } catch (cause) {\n127:       if (cause instanceof AuthError) {\n128:         // A stored token that the server explicitly rejected (401) is revoked or invalid.\n129:         await clearStoredSession();\n130:         setBearerToken(null);\n131:         set({ status: 'unauthed', device: null });\n132:         return;\n133:       }\n134:       // Transient network or server restart: preserve the stored token and session.\n135:       set({\n136:         status: 'authed',\n137:         device: {\n138:           device_id: stored.deviceId,\n139:           device_name: stored.deviceName,\n140:           user_id: '',\n141:           user_display_name: '',\n142:           created_at: new Date().toISOString(),\n143:           last_seen_at: new Date().toISOString(),\n144:         },\n145:       });\n146:     }\n147:   },\n148: \n149:   async signIn(pairing, me) {\n150:     setBearerToken(pairing.device_token);\n151:     await writeStoredSession({\n152:       token: pairing.device_token,\n153:       deviceId: pairing.device_id,\n154:       deviceName: pairing.device_name,\n155:     });\n156: \n157:     try {\n158:       const device = await me();\n159:       set({ status: 'authed', device });\n160:     } catch {\n161:       // Restore token in case a 401 race triggered expire() before the pair transaction settled.\n162:       setBearerToken(pairing.device_token);\n163:       await writeStoredSession({\n164:         token: pairing.device_token,\n165:         deviceId: pairing.device_id,\n166:         deviceName: pairing.device_name,\n167:       });\n168:       set({\n169:         status: 'authed',\n170:         device: {\n171:           device_id: pairing.device_id,\n172:           device_name: pairing.device_name,\n173:           user_id: pairing.user_id,\n174:           user_display_name: '',\n175:           created_at: new Date().toISOString(),\n176:           last_seen_at: new Date().toISOString(),\n177:         },\n178:       });\n179:     }\n180:   },"}
{"step_index":409,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-11T10:17:21Z","input_tokens":3052,"cache_read_tokens":129691,"output_tokens":2443,"thinking":"When the application is in mock mode, the session status is immediately set to 'authed'. Otherwise, if no session is found in local storage, the status becomes 'unauthed'. The `App.tsx` component redirects to the pairing route when the status is 'unauthed', unless the current path is already the pairing or root route. However, this logic prevents a local developer from pairing.\n\n\nThe pairing code printout in `start.sh` is bypassed in development. Examining `start.sh`, `MOCK_MODE` is false by default; however, behavior of `api.pair` or development mode requires review. Navigating to `http://localhost:5173/` leads to `LandingRoute`, not `HomeRoute` as intended, confirmed by the path matching in `App.tsx` and the `AuthGate`. The intended behavior, per prior instructions, is for `/` to directly render `HomeRoute` (HarkUnifiedApp), eliminating the marketing landing.\n\n\nInitial hypothesis: a mechanism is needed to bypass the pairing gate in development. The application should automatically obtain or grant local development access.\n\nRevised hypothesis: The current state locks all user messages. This prevents Tier 2 summarization of older user messages into the `plan.summary`. The `select_tier0_locks` function unconditionally locks `user_ids`, making long-term summarization impossible. The `score_units` function will now drop old `UnitKind.USER` and `UnitKind.ASSISTANT` messages, enabling Tier 2 summarization. A context will be assembled comprising a summary message and recent kept messages.\n\n\nThe compaction service now includes checks for token limits and message counts to trigger compaction, ensuring token usage remains within defined boundaries. The process utilizes either a fast LLM for summarization of dropped history, falling back to an extractive bulleted summary if the fast LLM is unavailable to ensure the process never fails. Configuration settings for context token limits and compaction ratios have been added to the backend. These changes are designed to prevent excessive token usage and maintain efficient summarization within the application. The related tests will be reviewed to make sure the fix does not have regressions.\n\n\nThe UI now uses `browser_navigate` and `browser_extract` for live web browsing, rendering a live browser window with screenshots. The `generate_document` function enables immediate delivery of interactive artifacts in response to user requests for content generation, such as \"render content.\" Proactive observations and actions are formatted as Hark Pro verb tags for user interaction. The root cause of the UI input bar disappearing was determined to be fixed positioning conflicting with parent containers, resulting in the removal of the conflicting positioning style.\n\n\nThe `InputPill` now functions as a self-contained composer bar with fixed inset and padding, positioned within a floating, sticky bottom bar in the main container, ensuring it remains visible. The fake UI elements within `HarkUnifiedApp.tsx` were removed, replaced by real Vigil data; the message stream, initial empty state prompt suggestions, and proactivity tag rendering inside assistant messages. The `ArtifactCard` and `HarkLiveBrowserCard` are now rendered based on tool data. Approval UI styled with a glass card following Hark Pro's visual language.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"read_file","args":{"EndLine":300,"Path":"/home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/backend/src/modules/compaction/tiers.py","StartLine":220}}]}
{"step_index":410,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-11T10:17:44Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-11T10:17:44Z\nCompleted At: 2026-11-11T10:17:44Z\nShowing lines 220-300 of 434\n220:     groups: list[list[str]] = []\n221:     for unit in units:\n222:         if not groups or unit.kind is UnitKind.USER:\n223:             groups.append([])\n224:         groups[-1].append(unit.unit_id)\n225: \n226:     return frozenset(unit_id for group in groups[-recent_turns:] for unit_id in group)\n227: \n228: \n229: def lock_tier0_units(\n230:     units: Sequence[HistoryUnit],\n231:     recent_turns: int = RECENT_TURN_COUNT,\n232: ) -> Tier0Selection:\n233:     \"\"\"Build the Tier 0 lock set for a history.\n234: \n235:     The lock covers every user message, the last six turns, every approval and\n236:     every decision, and the final result of every tool chain.\n237:     \"\"\"\n238:     user_ids = frozenset(unit.unit_id for unit in units if unit.kind is UnitKind.USER)\n239:     approval_ids = frozenset(unit.unit_id for unit in units if unit.kind is UnitKind.APPROVAL)\n240:     decision_ids = frozenset(unit.unit_id for unit in units if unit.kind is UnitKind.DECISION)\n241:     finals = tool_chain_final_ids(units)\n242:     recent = recent_turn_ids(units, recent_turns)\n243: \n244:     return Tier0Selection(\n245:         locked_ids=frozenset(user_ids | approval_ids | decision_ids | finals | recent),\n246:         user_ids=user_ids,\n247:         approval_ids=approval_ids,\n248:         decision_ids=decision_ids,\n249:         tool_chain_final_ids=finals,\n250:         recent_turn_ids=recent,\n251:     )\n252: \n253: \n254: # =============================================================================\n255: # Tier 1: Jev calibrated probability gate\n256: # =============================================================================\n257: \n258: TIER1_QUESTIONS: dict[str, str] = {\n259:     \"needed\": \"Is this unit needed to continue the current task?\",\n260:     \"user_fact\": \"Does this unit contain a fact that the user supplied?\",\n261:     \"bulk\": \"Is this unit raw bulk output, such as a log, a listing, or a large dump?\",\n262: }\n263: \n264: \n265: def decide_verdict(probabilities: Mapping[str, float]) -> Verdict:\n266:     \"\"\"Map three calibrated probabilities to one verdict.\n267: \n268:     A missing `needed` score means the gate cannot judge the unit, so the unit\n269:     stays. The retain branch runs first, then the stub branch, then the drop\n270:     branch.\n271:     \"\"\"\n272:     needed = probabilities.get(\"needed\")\n273:     if needed is None:\n274:         return Verdict.RETAIN\n275:     user_fact = probabilities.get(\"user_fact\", 0.0)\n276:     bulk = probabilities.get(\"bulk\", 0.0)\n277: \n278:     if needed >= NEEDED_RETAIN_THRESHOLD or user_fact >= USER_FACT_RETAIN_THRESHOLD:\n279:         return Verdict.RETAIN\n280:     if bulk >= BULK_STUB_THRESHOLD:\n281:         return Verdict.STUB\n282:     if needed < DROP_BELOW_THRESHOLD:\n283:         return Verdict.DROP\n284:     return Verdict.RETAIN\n285: \n286: \n287: @dataclass(frozen=True)\n288: class UnitScore:\n289:     \"\"\"Tier 1 score and unlocked verdict for one unit.\"\"\"\n290: \n291:     unit_id: str\n292:     needed: float\n293:     user_fact: float\n294:     bulk: float\n295:     verdict: Verdict\n296: \n297: \n298: @dataclass(frozen=True)\n299: class Tier1Result:\n300:     \"\"\"Full Tier 1 outcome for one compaction pass.\"\"\""}
