{"step_index":420,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-11T10:18:26Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-11T10:18:26Z\nCompleted At: 2026-11-11T10:18:27Z\nShowing lines 210-260 of 260\n210: \n211: def test_lock_set_is_the_union_of_the_rules() -> None:\n212:     \"\"\"The lock set is the union of users, approvals, decisions, finals, recent turns.\"\"\"\n213:     units = build_history()\n214:     selection = lock_tier0_units(units)\n215: \n216:     expected = (\n217:         selection.user_ids\n218:         | selection.approval_ids\n219:         | selection.decision_ids\n220:         | selection.tool_chain_final_ids\n221:         | selection.recent_turn_ids\n222:     )\n223:     assert selection.locked_ids == expected\n224:     assert selection.is_locked(\"t1-user\") is True\n225:     assert selection.is_locked(\"t1-tool-a\") is False\n226: \n227: \n228: def test_units_from_messages_maps_roles_and_locks() -> None:\n229:     \"\"\"Message dictionaries map to the right unit kinds for the lock.\"\"\"\n230:     from src.modules.compaction.tiers import units_from_messages\n231: \n232:     units = units_from_messages(\n233:         [\n234:             {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"Add the compaction module.\", \"id\": \"m1\"},\n235:             {\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": \"I will write tiers.py.\"},\n236:             {\n237:                 \"role\": \"tool\",\n238:                 \"content\": \"collected 12 items\",\n239:                 \"tool_name\": \"bash\",\n240:                 \"command\": \"pytest\",\n241:                 \"exit_code\": 0,\n242:                 \"artifact_id\": \"art-1\",\n243:             },\n244:             {\"role\": \"approval\", \"content\": \"approved\", \"kind\": \"approval\"},\n245:         ]\n246:     )\n247: \n248:     assert units[0].kind is UnitKind.USER\n249:     assert units[0].unit_id == \"m1\"\n250:     assert units[1].kind is UnitKind.ASSISTANT\n251:     assert units[2].kind is UnitKind.TOOL_RESULT\n252:     assert units[2].artifact_id == \"art-1\"\n253:     assert units[2].exit_code == 0\n254:     assert units[2].size_bytes == len(\"collected 12 items\")\n255:     assert units[3].kind is UnitKind.APPROVAL\n256: \n257:     selection = lock_tier0_units(units)\n258:     assert selection.is_locked(\"m1\") is True\n259:     assert selection.is_locked(\"unit-0003\") is True\n260:     assert selection.is_locked(\"unit-0001\") is True"}
{"step_index":421,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-11T10:18:27Z","input_tokens":2154,"cache_read_tokens":138233,"output_tokens":2271,"thinking":"Initial hypothesis: `selection.locked_ids` should represent a union of specific IDs. Observing `test_tier0.py` confirms this: the locked IDs equal a union of user, approval, decision, toolchain final, and recent turn IDs. Crucially, intermediate tool outputs like `t1-tool-a` are *not* locked in Tier 0. Tier 1's evaluation then determines if these unlocked items are retained or dropped based on thresholds.\n\n\nInitial suspicion was that intermediate tool outputs were being stubbed, but `_fallback_evaluate` always marked them as needed, preventing this. The token limit of 100,000 tokens in `loop.py` also prevented the compact check from ever being invoked, retaining all tool outputs and thoughts. The `_fallback_evaluate` function in `jev.py` needs adjustment to correctly identify and exclude intermediate tool results.\n\n\nThe logic for dropping or stubbing intermediate tool results is identified. The \"needed\" question probability being low (0.15) for unlocked items combined with the decision threshold (< 0.3) results in a drop verdict. This explains the artifact removal. This confirms the hypothesis about the mechanism of artifact removal through a combination of evaluation and verdict.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"edit_file","args":{"Path":"/home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/backend/src/integrations/jev/jev.py","Replacement":"        for q_key in questions:\n            q_lower = q_key.lower()\n            if \"bulk\" in q_lower:\n                content_bulk = len(str(state.get(\"content\", \"\"))) > 250 or state.get(\"kind\") in (\"tool_result\", \"tool\")\n                is_b = is_bulk or content_bulk\n                answers[q_key] = \"yes\" if is_b else \"no\"\n                probabilities[q_key] = 0.88 if is_b else 0.10\n            elif \"needed\" in q_lower:\n                # In compaction, unlocked intermediate outputs and old chatter can be summarized/dropped\n                is_n = state.get(\"kind\") in (\"approval\", \"decision\") or state.get(\"role\") == \"user\"\n                answers[q_key] = \"yes\" if is_n else \"no\"\n                probabilities[q_key] = 0.85 if is_n else 0.15\n            elif \"user_fact\" in q_lower:\n                is_u = state.get(\"role\") == \"user\" or \"user\" in str(state.get(\"kind\", \"\"))\n                answers[q_key] = \"yes\" if is_u else \"no\"\n                probabilities[q_key] = 0.90 if is_u else 0.05\n            elif any(k in q_lower for k in [\"urgent\", \"urgency\"]):\n                answers[q_key] = \"yes\" if is_urgent else \"no\"\n                probabilities[q_key] = 0.92 if is_urgent else 0.15\n            elif \"action\" in q_lower:\n                answers[q_key] = \"yes\" if is_actionable else \"no\"\n                probabilities[q_key] = 0.88 if is_actionable else 0.12\n            else:\n                answers[q_key] = \"no\"\n                probabilities[q_key] = 0.50","Target":"        for q_key in questions:\n            if \"bulk\" in q_key.lower():\n                answers[q_key] = \"yes\" if is_bulk else \"no\"\n                probabilities[q_key] = 0.95 if is_bulk else 0.05\n            elif any(k in q_key.lower() for k in [\"urgent\", \"urgency\"]):\n                answers[q_key] = \"yes\" if is_urgent else \"no\"\n                probabilities[q_key] = 0.92 if is_urgent else 0.15\n            elif \"action\" in q_key.lower():\n                answers[q_key] = \"yes\" if is_actionable else \"no\"\n                probabilities[q_key] = 0.88 if is_actionable else 0.12\n            else:\n                answers[q_key] = \"no\"\n                probabilities[q_key] = 0.50"}}]}
