{"step_index":555,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-11T10:31:23Z","input_tokens":2867,"cache_read_tokens":207682,"output_tokens":1256,"thinking":"The code comments describe a function called `history_with` that's designed to construct a history of turns. This suggests an interest in context management, specifically how prior interactions are assembled for use in a specific processing tier. Understanding how the target unit is positioned relative to the overall turn sequence is crucial.\n\n\nInitial hypothesis: Tier 0's locking mechanism was incorrectly bypassed, leading to incorrect stubbing/dropping of intermediate tool results. The previous code in `_fallback_evaluate` and `_StubJevClient` was assigning high \"needed\" values to intermediate tool results, preventing stubbing. Our fix changed these values, enabling stubbing. The `resolve_verdicts` function, crucial for enforcing Tier 0 locks, appears to be functioning as expected based on the initial assessment of its code. The plan is to revert the `resolve_verdicts` function to original state to observe if the previously unlocked results are unlocked once more.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"edit_file","args":{"Path":"/home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/backend/src/modules/compaction/tiers.py","Replacement":"def resolve_verdicts(\n    units: Sequence[HistoryUnit],\n    tier1: Tier1Result,\n    tier0: Tier0Selection,\n) -> dict[str, Verdict]:\n    \"\"\"Apply the Tier 0 lock to every Tier 1 verdict.\n\n    This function is the single place where the safety lock is enforced. A\n    locked unit keeps the verdict RETAIN whatever Tier 1 says.\n    \"\"\"\n    resolved: dict[str, Verdict] = {}\n    for unit in units:\n        if tier0.is_locked(unit.unit_id):\n            resolved[unit.unit_id] = Verdict.RETAIN\n            continue\n        score = tier1.score_for(unit.unit_id)\n        resolved[unit.unit_id] = Verdict.RETAIN if score is None else score.verdict\n    return resolved","Target":"def resolve_verdicts(\n    units: Sequence[HistoryUnit],\n    tier1: Tier1Result,\n    tier0: Tier0Selection,\n) -> dict[str, Verdict]:\n    \"\"\"Apply the Tier 0 lock to every Tier 1 verdict.\n\n    This function is the single place where the safety lock is enforced.\n    Approvals, decisions, and recent conversation turns are strictly locked.\n    Historical tool results and assistant progress messages outside the recent\n    turns are judged by Tier 1 to allow stubbing and summarization.\n    \"\"\"\n    resolved: dict[str, Verdict] = {}\n    for unit in units:\n        score = tier1.score_for(unit.unit_id)\n        if unit.kind in (UnitKind.APPROVAL, UnitKind.DECISION) or unit.unit_id in tier0.recent_turn_ids:\n            resolved[unit.unit_id] = Verdict.RETAIN\n            continue\n        if unit.kind is UnitKind.USER:\n            resolved[unit.unit_id] = Verdict.RETAIN\n            continue\n        if score is not None:\n            resolved[unit.unit_id] = score.verdict\n        elif tier0.is_locked(unit.unit_id):\n            resolved[unit.unit_id] = Verdict.RETAIN\n        else:\n            resolved[unit.unit_id] = Verdict.RETAIN\n    return resolved"}}]}
