{"step_index":571,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-11T10:33:16Z","input_tokens":3261,"cache_read_tokens":215190,"output_tokens":2702,"content":"### 1. Root Cause Analysis & Resolution\n\n#### A. Why Compaction Failed (The \"Context Issue & Ridiculous Input Token Bill\")\n* **The Root Cause**:\n  1. **Zero-Drop Fallback**: When running locally without an external Jev API key (`JEV_API_KEY=\"\"`), both `JevClient._fallback_evaluate` and `_StubJevClient` were returning `probabilities[\"needed\"] = 0.50` (or `0.90`). In `decide_verdict()`, any score $\\ge 0.30$ and $< 0.70$ defaults to `Verdict.RETAIN`. Because nothing was ever scored $< 0.30$, **100% of historical units were retained forever**.\n  2. **100,000 Token Gate**: In [`loop.py`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/backend/src/modules/runs/loop.py), `RunLoop` had `context_token_limit = 100_000` with `compact_ratio = 0.70`, meaning compaction was never even evaluated until a run reached **70,000 tokens**.\n  3. Consequently, every previous turn's thoughts, intermediate bash outputs, and web dumps re-entered the context window on every single turn, blowing up input token bills.\n* **The Fix**:\n  * Added `CONTEXT_TOKEN_LIMIT: int = 8_000` in [`settings.py`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/backend/src/config/settings.py) and wired it into [`service.py`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/backend/src/modules/runs/service.py) and [`loop.py`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/backend/src/modules/runs/loop.py). Compaction now evaluates when tokens pass ~5,600 or when history exceeds 10 turns.\n  * Corrected `_fallback_evaluate` and `_StubJevClient` to score older intermediate tool outputs and routine thoughts as drop/stub candidates (`needed: 0.15`, `bulk: 0.88`).\n  * Bulk outputs (such as 1,400-token bash logs) are now converted into compact 86-token [`ArtifactStub`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/backend/src/modules/compaction/stub.py) references, and Tier 2 Fast LLM synthesizes an executive summary block at the head of context.\n  * Validated with unit test [`test_compaction_effectiveness.py`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/backend/tests/unit/test_compaction_effectiveness.py) (All 27 compaction tests passing).\n\n---\n\n#### B. Why the Agent Was Oblivious to What It Can Do\n* **The Root Cause**:\n  * In [`core_context.py`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/backend/src/modules/runs/core_context.py), `DEFAULT_BASE_IDENTITY` told the agent it only had basic `/workspace` file reads and searches. It instructed the agent to stall and ask questions (`ask_user`) on broad requests, leading the agent to ask *\"What content do you want me to render, and in which format?\"* and trigger an approval with empty arguments (`action_execution`).\n* **The Fix**:\n  * Updated `DEFAULT_BASE_IDENTITY` in [`core_context.py`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/backend/src/modules/runs/core_context.py) with full awareness of:\n    1. **Immediate Artifact Generation**: When asked to \"render content\", \"show a prototype\", or \"build a website\", do not stall with `ask_user`. Immediately call `generate_document` (`html`, `markdown`, etc.) or `deliver_file`. The UI automatically renders them in an interactive sandboxed viewport.\n    2. **Cloud Browser Execution**: The agent now actively uses `browser_navigate` and `browser_extract` (Firecrawl) to visit URLs, inspect pages, and return live screenshot cards.\n    3. **Proactivity Verb Tags**: Structured tags format `[Verb] Description...` (e.g. `[Accept] 5:30 PM Maji invite...`, `[Draft] note to reschedule...`, `[Build] interactive widget`).\n    4. **Execution Hygiene**: Explicit instructions preventing tool invocations with empty/missing arguments.\n\n---\n\n#### C. Eliminating the Mock Overlay & Restoring the Real Floating Input Field\n* **The Root Cause of \"Creating an overlay as opposed to utilizing components properly\"**:\n  * The earlier implementation hardcoded static mock cards (Boardy's invite, static Cloudflare sign-in screenshot, fake Hark Pro limit card) inside `HarkUnifiedApp.tsx` that vanished once a real message was sent.\n  * In [`InputPill.tsx`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/components/chat/InputPill.tsx), a legacy `pointer-events-none fixed inset-x-0 bottom-28 md:pl-20` clashed with the flex container. When messages expanded, the container pushed the composer off-screen, making the input field disappear.\n* **The Fix**:\n  * **Removed All Mock Overlays**: [`HarkUnifiedApp.tsx`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/components/hark/HarkUnifiedApp.tsx) now binds directly to live Vigil session data, real [`MessageStream`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/components/chat/MessageStream.tsx), real [`ArtifactCard`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/components/chat/ArtifactCard.tsx), and real browser cards.\n  * **Guaranteed Visible Floating Composer**:\n    * Cleaned up [`InputPill.tsx`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/components/chat/InputPill.tsx) into a self-contained, auto-expanding composer.\n    * Pinned it in a fixed floating layer at the bottom of the screen (`fixed bottom-6 z-40 left-0 right-0 md:left-[300px] flex justify-center px-4 pointer-events-none`). The textarea and buttons have `pointer-events-auto` and are **always visible and interactive**, regardless of message scroll height.\n  * **Sleek Action Approvals**: Updated [`InlineApprovalCard.tsx`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/components/chat/InlineApprovalCard.tsx) to replace the ugly code block with Hark Pro rounded pill buttons (`[Approve]` in solid accent, `[Reject]` in bordered pill) and clean descriptive action copy.\n  * **Unified Landing**: In [`App.tsx`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/App.tsx), `/` now maps directly to [`HomeRoute`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/routes/HomeRoute.tsx) (the Hark Pro Canvas), and [`PairRoute.tsx`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/routes/PairRoute.tsx) includes a developer bypass so testing never gets stuck on pairing gates.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Verification & Test Status\n* **Frontend**: `pnpm typecheck` passed (0 errors), `pnpm build` completed in **1.36s** (`dist/` generated cleanly).\n* **Backend**: All **665 unit and integration tests passed** in **51.94s** (`uv run pytest tests/unit/`).","thinking":"Frontend and backend are fully built, passing all tests. Confirmed the compaction issue was due to Tier 1 heuristic fallbacks returning values leading to an incorrect verdict mapping, as indicated by the specific code locations.\n\n\nThe compaction issue was resolved by addressing the incorrect verdict mapping in Tier 1 heuristics and setting sensible thresholds for token counts and turn limits, ensuring automatic compaction. Verified through new tests that large logs are effectively compacted, triggering the Tier 2 summarizer and maintaining tight context. Updated the agent's identity to fully utilize interactive artifact rendering, cloud browser navigation, active verb tags for UI interaction, and Groq Whisper voice STT, enforcing strict rules against empty tool arguments.\n\n\n"}
