on. \n  - [Attachment: image/png (/home/nasbombz/.gemini/antigravity/brain/4c9225c7-9a87-4aee-bca4-891ac270da2a/.user_uploaded/media_1794336791572_accff37b.jpg)]\n  - [Attachment: image/png (/home/nasbombz/.gemini/antigravity/brain/4c9225c7-9a87-4aee-bca4-891ac270da2a/.user_uploaded/media_1794336809063_d470144a.jpg)]\n  - [Attachment: image/png (/home/nasbombz/.gemini/antigravity/brain/4c9225c7-9a87-4aee-bca4-891ac270da2a/.user_uploaded/media_1794336824522_aacb669d.jpg)]\n  - [Attachment: image/png (/home/nasbombz/.gemini/antigravity/brain/4c9225c7-9a87-4aee-bca4-891ac270da2a/.user_uploaded/media_1794336846627_6550ceb2.jpg)]\n  - [Attachment: image/png (/home/nasbombz/.gemini/antigravity/brain/4c9225c7-9a87-4aee-bca4-891ac270da2a/.user_uploaded/media_1794336863617_4cdbb3cc.jpg)]\n  - [Attachment: image/png (/home/nasbombz/.gemini/antigravity/brain/4c9225c7-9a87-4aee-bca4-891ac270da2a/.user_uploaded/media_1794336878629_d2da638e.jpg)]\n  - [Attachment: image/png (/home/nasbombz/.gemini/antigravity/brain/4c9225c7-9a87-4aee-bca4-891ac270da2a/.user_uploaded/media_1794336895259_12128f2c.jpg)]\n  - [Attachment: image/png (/home/nasbombz/.gemini/antigravity/brain/4c9225c7-9a87-4aee-bca4-891ac270da2a/.user_uploaded/media_1794336932722_469fb2f7.jpg)]\n  - [Attachment: image/png (/home/nasbombz/.gemini/antigravity/brain/4c9225c7-9a87-4aee-bca4-891ac270da2a/.user_uploaded/media_1794336946036_b6bb06a4.jpg)]\n  - [Attachment omitted due to token budget: image/png (/home/nasbombz/.gemini/antigravity/brain/4c9225c7-9a87-4aee-bca4-891ac270da2a/.user_uploaded/media_1794337031632_c639a127.jpg)]\n4. continue\n5. continue\n6. It seems like the chnage cant reflect in the UI\n7. Also the agent is obliviou to all the changes and what it can do. Lastly the cotext issue is insane. The compaction doent dork so the token input token bill is rediculous\n8. There was no input field?\n  - [Attachment: image/png (/home/nasbombz/.gemini/antigravity/brain/4c9225c7-9a87-4aee-bca4-891ac270da2a/.user_uploaded/media_1794391444891_7c59dde6.jpg)]\n9. You are creating an iverlay as oposed to creating and utilizing the components properly\n10. The chat mesage i seent to the ui didnt reach the backend \n\n<summary>\n## 1. Task Overview\n- **User's Core Request**:\n  1. Fix the chat message transmission failure: Messages sent from the UI composer did not reach the backend.\n  2. Eliminate the mock overlay in favor of real component architecture (no hardcoded fake Hark screenshots masking the real Vigil system).\n  3. Ensure the input field (`InputPill`) is always present, pinned, and interactive.\n  4. Fix context compaction so it actually reduces history tokens instead of inflating LLM input token bills.\n  5. Ensure the agent system prompt is fully aware of its Hark Pro capabilities (immediate artifact generation, live cloud browser execution with Firecrawl, structured verb tags, voice dictation, no spurious approvals with empty arguments).\n- **Scope & Constraints**:\n  - Keep 100% test pass rates across both Python unit/integration tests and TypeScript typechecking/Vite builds.\n  - Maintain the warm sand/peach (light) and moody charcoal/plum (dark) Hark Pro aesthetic.\n  - Do not use static mock overlays or re-introduce the legacy floating dock / cartoon mascot.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Progress\n- **Compaction Pipeline Fully Repaired & Verified**:\n  - Identified root causes: `_StubJevClient` and `_fallback_evaluate` in `backend/src/integrations/jev/jev.py` and `backend/src/dependencies.py` were returning `needed: 0.50` or `0.90` on all units, which mapped to `Verdict.RETAIN` for 100% of history units (zero dropped/stubbed units). Furthermore, `context_token_limit` in `RunLoop` was set to `100_000` tokens.\n  - Fixed `_fallback_evaluate` and `_StubJevClient` to score older intermediate tool outputs and routine thoughts as drop/stub candidates (`needed: 0.15`, `bulk: 0.88`).\n  - Added `CONTEXT_TOKEN_LIMIT: int = 8_000` in `backend/src/config/settings.py` and passed it into `RunLoop` (`service.py` & `loop.py`). Compaction triggers when context exceeds ~5,600 tokens or history exceeds 10 turns.\n  - Reverted `resolve_verdicts` in `backend/src/modules/compaction/tiers.py` to preserve Tier 0 safety locks strictly as required by the specifications.\n  - Added unit test `backend/tests/unit/test_compaction_effectiveness.py` which passes and proves bulk tool outputs are stubbed from 1,401 tokens down to 86 tokens with Tier 2 fast LLM executive summary generated.\n  - Backend test results: **665 passed, 1 xfailed in 51.94s** across all unit and integration tests.\n- **Agent Awareness & System Prompt**:\n  - Updated `DEFAULT_BASE_IDENTITY` in `backend/src/modules/runs/core_context.py` to make the agent aware of its live canvas capabilities: immediate artifact generation without stalling on `ask_user`, live browser execution via Firecrawl, active verb tags `[Verb] Description...`, Groq Whisper voice STT, and strict tool execution hygiene.\n- **Frontend Living Canvas & Input Field**:\n  - Replaced fake mock overlay cards in `web/src/components/hark/HarkUnifiedApp.tsx` with authentic Hark Pro living canvas:\n    - Empty state: Clean greeting (\"How can I help you today?\") with clickable verb prompt pills (`[Draft]`, `[Build]`, `[Browse]`).\n    - Active state: Real `MessageStream`, `ThinkingCapsule`, and `ArtifactCard`.\n  - Pinned `InputPill` as a floating composer (`fixed bottom-6 left-0 right-0 md:left-[300px] z-40 pointer-events-none` with `pointer-events-auto` inner pill) so it is **always visible and interactive**.\n  - Updated `InlineApprovalCard.tsx` with Hark Pro double-bezel pill buttons (`[Approve]`, `[Reject]`) and clean descriptive copy.\n  - Updated `web/src/App.tsx` so `/` routes directly to `HomeRoute`.\n  - Frontend verified: `pnpm typecheck` passed (0 errors), `pnpm build` completed in **1.36s**.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Key Findings: Why Chat Messages Did Not Reach the Backend\nThrough live tracing of the request path (`InputPill` $\\rightarrow$ `chat.send()` $\\rightarrow$ `api.createRun` $\\rightarrow$ FastAPI):\n1. **Missing Bearer Token / 422 Header Validation Error**:\n   - `get_current_device` in `backend/src/modules/auth/dependencies.py` declares:\n     `authorization: str = Header(..., description=\"Device Bearer token: 'Bearer vgt_...'\")`\n   - Because `Header(...)` has `...` (Ellipsis), FastAPI marks `Authorization` as **strictly required**.\n   - On a fresh browser load where IndexedDB has no stored token, requests to `/runs/configs/default`, `/chat/sessions`, and `/runs` send no `Authorization` header.\n   - FastAPI intercepts the request before reaching route handlers and throws:\n     `422 Unprocessable Entity: {\"details\": [{\"loc\": [\"header\", \"authorization\"], \"msg\": \"Field required\"}]}`.\n2. **Silent Drop in `useAgentChat.send()`**:\n   - In `web/src/queries/chat.ts`:\n     ```ts\n     const target = sessionIdRef.current;\n     if (!trimmed || !target) return; // Silent drop if target is null\n\n     const configId = defaultConfig.data?.id;\n     if (!configId) {\n       setError('The agent configuration is not ready yet. Try again in a moment.');\n       return; // Bails out if default config failed or is still loading\n     }\n     ```\n   - Because `api.listSessions()` and `api.getDefaultAgentConfig()` failed with 422, `activeSessionId` was `null` and `configId` was `undefined`.\n   - When the user clicked Send, `chat.send(draft)` returned immediately without making any network call, and `HarkUnifiedApp.tsx` was not displaying `chat.error`.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Errors & Fixes\n- **Error 1: `relation \"pairing_codes\" does not exist`**:\n  - *Details*: Attempting to query `pairing_codes` via raw SQL threw an undefined table error.\n  - *Fix*: Pairing codes in Vigil's design are transiently held in memory (`PAIRING_CODES` dict in `backend/src/modules/auth/state.py`), while `devices` and `users` are persistent tables in PostgreSQL.\n- **Error 2: Tier 0 / Tier 1 Test Regression during Compaction Tuning**:\n  - *Details*: Modifying `resolve_verdicts` to unlock tool finals caused 6 unit tests in `test_tier0.py` and `test_tier1.py` to fail (`Left contains one more item: 't1-tool-final'`).\n  - *Fix*: Reverted `resolve_verdicts` to adhere strictly to the specification. Fixed compaction by scoring unlocked intermediate units in `_fallback_evaluate` and `_StubJevClient` with `needed: 0.15` and `bulk: 0.88`, which preserved all tests (665 passing).\n- **Error 3: Header Validation 422 on Unauthenticated Dev Requests**:\n  - *Details*: `curl -i http://localhost:5173/api/v1/runs/configs/default` returned 422 because `authorization` header is mandatory.\n  - *Root Cause Identified*: Unpaired browser sessions in development get blocked before route execution.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Active Context\n- **Workspace**: `/home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent`\n- **Processes Running**:\n  - Uvicorn on port 8000 (PID ~113794 / 113800)\n  - Worker process (PID ~56858)\n  - Vite dev server on port 5173 (PID ~56895)\n- **Database**: PostgreSQL 16 + pgvector on localhost:5432/vigil (Alembic at head: 0009).\n\n---\n\n## 6. Next Steps (Immediate Resumption Checklist)\n\n### Step 1: Fix Development Authentication in Backend & Web Client\n1. In `backend/src/modules/auth/dependencies.py` and `backend/src/dependencies.py`:\n   - Change `authorization: str = Header(...)` to `authorization: str | None = Header(None)`.\n   - In `get_current_device`, if `authorization` is missing or is `\"Bearer dev\"` and `settings.APP_ENV in (\"development\", \"test\")`:\n     - Seamlessly resolve to a default local device using `service.get_or_create_default_device()`.\n     - In production (`settings.APP_ENV == \"production\"`), raise `UnauthorizedError(\"Missing bearer token\")`.\n   - In `backend/src/modules/auth/service.py`:\n     - Implement `get_or_create_default_device()`: gets or creates default user `\"Local User\"` and returns an active `DeviceDTO`.\n2. In `web/src/lib/api.ts`:\n   - If `bearerToken` is absent and `import.meta.env.DEV`, default header to `Bearer dev` so requests pass smoothly.\n3. Test with `curl -i http://localhost:5173/api/v1/runs/configs/default` and verify it returns **200 OK**.\n\n### Step 2: Make `chat.send()` Robust Against Empty Sessions\n1. In `web/src/queries/chat.ts`:\n   - In `send(prompt: string, overrideSessionId?: string)`:\n     - If `target` is not set, allow passing `overrideSessionId`.\n     - If `defaultConfig.data?.id` is not yet available, fallback to awaiting `api.getDefaultAgentConfig()`.\n2. In `web/src/components/hark/HarkUnifiedApp.tsx`:\n   - Update composer submission handler:\n     ```ts\n     const handleSend = async (text: string) => {\n       let sid = activeSessionId;\n       if (!sid) {\n         const newSession = await createSession.mutateAsync({\n           title: text.slice(0, 35),\n           scope: `chat:create-session:${Date.now()}`,\n         });\n         sid = newSession.session_id;\n         setCreatedSessionId(sid);\n       }\n       chat.send(text, sid);\n     };\n     ```\n   - Display `chat.error` inline if any transmission error occurs so failures are never silent.\n\n### Step 3: Run Full Validation & Dev Server Test\n1. Run `cd web && pnpm typecheck && pnpm build` (verify 0 errors).\n2. Run `uv run --directory backend pytest tests/unit/` (verify 665+ passing).\n3. Send a test message from `http://localhost:5173/` and verify in the backend uvicorn terminal that `POST /api/v1/runs` is logged and the agent executes and streams the reply.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Commitments & Constraints\n- Keep all unit and integration tests at 100% pass rate.\n- Adhere strictly to Hark Pro living canvas design specifications.\n- Never re-introduce static mock overlays.\n</summary>\n\nYou have the 13 following artifacts written to the artifacts directory:\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1794336791572_accff37b]\nPath: file:///home/nasbombz/.gemini/antigravity/brain/4c9225c7-9a87-4aee-bca4-891ac270da2a/.us