{"step_index":882,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-11T11:01:00Z","input_tokens":2250,"cache_read_tokens":145608,"output_tokens":1657,"content":"### Why Chat Messages Did Not Reach the Backend\n\nWe diagnosed the exact network and client execution trace for chat submissions:\n\n1. **FastAPI Header Validation Failure (422)**:\n   In `backend/src/modules/auth/dependencies.py` and `backend/src/dependencies.py`, `get_current_device` was declared with `authorization: str = Header(...)`. Because of the `...` (Ellipsis), FastAPI rejected any request without an explicit `Authorization` header with a `422 Unprocessable Entity: {\"details\": [{\"loc\": [\"header\", \"authorization\"], \"msg\": \"Field required\"}]}` before route handlers could execute.\n2. **Missing Session / Default Config Guard**:\n   In `web/src/queries/chat.ts`, `send()` bailed out early if `sessionIdRef.current` was `null` or if `defaultConfig.data?.id` had not finished loading. Because the initial bootstrap queries failed with 422 on an unpaired browser session, `chat.send()` silently returned without dispatching `POST /api/v1/runs`.\n\n---\n\n### Changes Applied\n\n#### 1. Backend Authentication & Dev Seeding\n- **Dependencies** ([`dependencies.py`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/backend/src/dependencies.py#L133-L144), [`auth/dependencies.py`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/backend/src/modules/auth/dependencies.py#L21-L32)):\n  - Updated `authorization: str | None = Header(None)`.\n  - Missing headers in production strictly return HTTP `401 Unauthorized` (`MISSING_TOKEN`), satisfying all security specifications.\n  - In development and test environments, unauthenticated requests or `\"Bearer dev\"` / `\"vgt_testtoken\"` automatically resolve to the local device via `AuthService.get_or_create_default_device()`.\n- **Auth Service** ([`auth/service.py`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/backend/src/modules/auth/service.py#L115-L130)):\n  - Implemented `get_or_create_default_device()` to ensure the default local user and active test device exist.\n\n#### 2. Frontend Request Pipeline & Auto Session Creation\n- **API Client & Session Hydration** ([`api.ts`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/lib/api.ts#L111-L113), [`useSession.ts`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/store/useSession.ts#L115-L126)):\n  - In development mode (`import.meta.env.DEV`), `api.request()` and `useSession.hydrate()` automatically use the local dev token so browser requests immediately authenticate with `200 OK`.\n- **Robust Message Sending** ([`queries/chat.ts`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/queries/chat.ts#L225-L270)):\n  - Updated `send(prompt, overrideSessionId)` to auto-create a chat session if no active session exists.\n  - Added dynamic fallback to fetch `api.getDefaultAgentConfig()` if not already cached.\n  - Exposed actionable inline error banners with a 1-click **Retry** button in [`HarkUnifiedApp.tsx`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/components/hark/HarkUnifiedApp.tsx#L235-L248).\n- **Clean Approval UI** ([`InlineApprovalCard.tsx`](file:///home/nasbombz/Documents/Projects/vigil-agent/web/src/components/chat/InlineApprovalCard.tsx#L68-L81)):\n  - Fixed empty tool arguments so rather than displaying `// No arguments passed`, it displays a clean explanation: *\"The agent is requesting authorization to execute this action.\"*\n\n---\n\n### Verification Results\n\n1. **End-to-End Live Run Flow Tested**:\n   - Sent a live message via API to verify the full loop:\n     ```\n     POST /api/v1/chat/sessions -> session bed6ef68-fd14-4e76-913d-25ec04a5f0c0\n     POST /api/v1/runs          -> run d8d05ebc-7b60-4ecf-b0f2-c7b227d56368\n     ```\n   - Worker picked up the run, executed the prompt `\"What is 2 + 2?\"`, compacted context, and returned `\"2 + 2 equals 4.\"` into the session messages.\n2. **Backend Test Suite**:\n   - **665 unit tests passed**, 1 xfailed (0 failures).\n   - **157 integration tests passed** (0 failures).\n3. **Frontend Build**:\n   - `tsc --noEmit` passed with 0 errors.\n   - `vite build` completed cleanly in 2.04s.","thinking":"The chat message transmission failure stemmed from a header validation issue in `get_current_device`. Unauthenticated developer requests triggered a 422 validation error because of the strict header declaration, blocking access to `api.me()` and `api.getDefaultAgent()`. This failure, in turn, prevented the subsequent transmission steps.\n\n\n"}
